Tens:1 \u219210  \nOnes:3 \u21923  \n\nAdding those up:\n\n1,000,000,000 + 300,000,000 = 1,300,000,000  \n+90,000,000 \u21921,390,000,000  \n+2,000,000 \u21921,392,000,000  \n+600,000 \u21921,392,600,000  \n+70,000 \u21921,392,670,000  \n+0 \u2192 same  \n+0 \u2192 same  \n+10 \u21921,392,670,010  \n+3 \u21921,392,670,013.\n\nWait, so the total is 1,392,670,013?\n\nBut let me verify this with another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake in the addition steps.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I should use another approach, like adding the numbers in parts.\n\nFirst, let's break down both numbers:\n\n522,632,563 can be written as:\n\n500,000,000 + 22,632,563  \nWait, but maybe splitting into millions:\n\n522,632,563 = 522,000,000 + 632,563  \n870,037,450 = 870,000,000 + 37,450  \n\nAdding those:\n\n522,000,000 + 870,000,000 = 1,392,000,000  \nThen 632,563 +37,450 = ?\n\nCalculating 632,563 +37,450:\n\n632,563 + 30,000 = 662,563  \n662,563 +7,450 = 669,013  \nSo total addition: 1,392,000,000 + 669,013 = 1,392,669,013?\n\nWait a minute, that's conflicting with the previous result of 1,392,670,013.\n\nHmm, so there's a discrepancy here. Which means I made a mistake somewhere.\n\nLet me recalculate the second method:\n\nFirst part: 522,632,563 + 870,037,450  \nBreaking into:\n\n522,632,563 + 870,037,450 = ?\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 522,632,563 + 870,037,450 step by step:\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n522,632,563  \n+870,037,450  \n= (522,632,563 + 800,000,000) + 70,037,450  \n= 1,322,632,563 + 70,037,450  \nNow, 1,322,632,563 +70,000,000 =1,392,632,563  \nThen adding 37,450: 1,392,632,563 +37,450 =1,392,670,013.\n\nAh, okay, so that matches the first method. So I must have made a mistake in the second approach when I split it into 522,000,000 + 870,000,000 and the remaining parts. Let me check that again.\n\nWait, in the second approach, I split 522,632,563 into 522,000,000 + 632,563 and 870,037,450 into 870,000,000 + 37,450. Then adding those gives:\n\n522,000,000 +870