es):8.\nPosition2 (tens):8.\nPosition3 (hundreds):0.\nPosition4 (thousands):9.\nPosition5 (ten thousands):9.\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):1.\nPosition7 (millions):7.\nPosition8 (ten millions):0.\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5.\nPosition10 (billions):0 (since it's a 9-digit number).\n\nNow adding each position step by step, starting from the rightmost (ones place):.\n\nPosition1 (ones): 7 + 8 =15 → write 5, carryover 1.\nPosition2 (tens):7 +8 +1 (carry) =16 → write 6, carryover 1. Wait wait, earlier I thought the tens place was 7+0 but maybe I made a mistake here. Let me redo the positions carefully.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the digit positions earlier. Let me re-express each number as digits in each place properly.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically aligned:.\n\nFirst number:  9 9 9 4 7 4 6 7 7.\n               (hundred millions, ten millions, millions, hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands, hundreds, tens, ones?).\n\nWait, perhaps it's better to separate each digit with commas as per standard:.\n\n999,474,677 is:.\n\nDigit positions (from right, starting at 1):.\n\n1 (ones):7.\n\n2 (tens):7.\n\n3 (hundreds):6.\n\n4 (thousands):4.\n\n5 (ten thousands):7.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):4.\n\n7 (millions):9.\n\n8 (ten millions):9.\n\n9 (hundred millions):9.\n\n10 (billions):0.\n\nSecond number:507,199,088 is:.\n\n1 (ones):8.\n\n2 (tens):8.\n\n3 (hundreds):0.\n\n4 (thousands):9.\n\n5 (ten thousands):9.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):1.\n\n7 (millions):7.\n\n8 (ten millions):0.\n\n9 (hundred millions):5.\n\n10 (billions):0.\n\nSo adding each position:.\n\nStarting from position 1 (ones):.\n\n7 +8 =15 → digit 5, carryover 1.\n\nPosition2 (tens):.\n\n7 (from first) +8 (from second) +1 (carry) = 16 → digit 6, carryover1.\n\nWait, that's different from my first calculation. Previously I thought the second number's tens digit was 0, but no, in the second number, the tens place is 8 (since the last two digits are 88). So the tens digit is 8. So that's where I messed up ear