has 3. Adding the carried 1: 4 + 3 + 1 = 8. So that's 8 here.\n\nAre there any more digits? The first number is 9 digits, the second also 9, so that should be all. Let me check each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nWait, let me recount the places to ensure alignment:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones: 2 +1 =3 ✔️.\n2. Tens: 2 +1 =3 ✔️.\n3. Hundreds:4+5=9 ✔️.\n4. Thousands:4+8=12 (write 2, carry 1) ✔️.\n5. Ten thousands:6+4 +1(carry)=11 (write 1, carry 1) ✔️.\n6. Hundred thousands:2+1 +1=4 ✔️.\n7. Millions:7+8=15 (write 5, carry 1) ✔️.\n8. Ten millions:1+9 +1(carry)=11 (write 1, carry 1) ✔️.\n9. Hundred millions:4+3 +1=8 ✔️.\n\nPutting all together: 8 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 3 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
