sition5:3\n\nPosition6:8\n\nPosition7:8\n\nPosition8:0\n\nPosition9:9\n\nSecond number:580931369\n\nDigits from right (position1 to 9):\n\nPosition1:9\n\nPosition2:6\n\nPosition3:3\n\nPosition4:1\n\nPosition5:3\n\nPosition6:9\n\nPosition7:0\n\nPosition8:8\n\nPosition9:5\n\nNow adding each position:\n\nPosition1:6+9=15 \u21925, carryover1\n\nPosition2:1+6=7 +1=8 \u21928, carryover0\n\nPosition3:4+3=7 \u21927, carryover0\n\nPosition4:5+1=6 \u21926, carryover0\n\nPosition5:3+3=6 \u21926, carryover0\n\nPosition6:8+9=17 \u21927, carryover1\n\nPosition7:8+0=8 +1=9 \u21929, carryover0\n\nPosition8:0+8=8 \u21928, carryover0\n\nPosition9:9+5=14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nThen the final carryover1 \u2192 position10:1.\n\nSo the digits from position1 to 10 are:\n\n5 (pos1), 8 (pos2),7 (pos3),6 (pos4),6 (pos5),7 (pos6),9 (pos7),8 (pos8),4 (pos9),1 (pos10).\n\nSo writing them in order from position10 to position1:\n\n1 (billion),4 (hundred millions),8 (ten millions),9 (millions),7 (hundred thousands),6 (ten thousands),6 (thousands),7 (hundreds),8 (tens),5 (ones).\n\nWait, hold on, the positions are numbered from right, so:\n\nPosition1: ones \u21925\n\nPosition2: tens \u21928\n\nPosition3: hundreds \u21927\n\nPosition4: thousands \u21926\n\nPosition5: ten thousands \u21926\n\nPosition6: hundred thousands \u21927\n\nPosition7: millions \u21929\n\nPosition8: ten millions \u21928\n\nPosition9: hundred millions \u21924\n\nPosition10: billions \u21921\n\nTherefore, the number is:\n\n1 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions), 9 (millions),7 (hundred thousands),6 (ten thousands),6 (thousands),7 (hundreds),8 (tens),5 (ones).\n\nWait, so when written out:\n\n1,489,766,785.\n\nAh! So in the digit-by-digit breakdown, the million's place is position7:9, which is millions. The hundred thousands place (position6) is7. So the number is 1,489,766,785. Wait, so previously when I thought it was 1,489,767,785, that was a mistake in transcribing the digits. The seventh digit from the right i