e write each digit position:.\n\nLet's list each digit from right to left (since addition starts from the right):.\n\nFirst number (282,911,059):.\nPosition 1 (ones): 9.\nPosition 2 (tens): 5.\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 0.\nPosition 4 (thousands): 1.\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 1.\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 9.\nPosition 7 (millions): 2.\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 8.\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 2.\n\nSecond number (281,026,748):.\nPosition 1 (ones): 8.\nPosition 2 (tens): 4.\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 7.\nPosition 4 (thousands): 6.\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 2.\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 0.\nPosition 7 (millions): 1.\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 8.\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 2.\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\nStarting from position 1 (ones):.\n9 + 8 = 17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):.\n5 + 4 = 9, plus 1 carried over = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):.\n0 +7 =7, plus 1 carried over =8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):.\n1 +6 =7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):.\n1 +2 =3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):.\n9 +0 =9. Write 9, no carryover.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):.\n2 +1 =3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):.\n8 +8 =16. Write 6, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):.\n2 +2 =4, plus the carried over 1 makes 5. Write 5.\n\nPutting all the digits together from last to first (since we started from the right):.\n\nThe digits from position 1 to 9 (right to left) are: 7,0,8,7,3,9,3,6,5. Wait, no. Wait, when we write the final number, the first digit we calculated (position 1) is the ones place, so the digits should be arranged as:.\n\nThe carried over from the highest position (position 9) gives the first digit. Let me list the digits in order:.\n\nStarting from the highest position (hundred millions place):.\n\nPosition 9: 5 (since 2+2+1=5).\nPosition 8: 6.\nPosition7:3.\nPosition6:9.\nPosition5:3.\nPosition4:7.\nPosition3:8.\nPosition2:0.\nPosition1:7.\n\nWait, but when you write the number, the order is from highest to lowest place value. So the final number would be:.\n\n5 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 7 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
