hundred millions (the first digit is 5 hundred million). The second number is 397,622,729, which is also 9 digits. So when adding, the billions place would actually be the first digit's sum? Wait no, because each number is less than a billion. Wait 591 million plus 397 million would be around 988 million. Wait, so the total sum is less than a billion? Wait, let me confirm:.\n\nWait, 591,525,997 plus 397,622,729. Let me add the millions first. 591 million plus 397 million is 988 million. Then adding the remaining parts: 525,997 + 622,729. Let's see, 525k plus 622k is 1,147,000. Then adding the 997 and 729 gives 1,726</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
