it2:9 (ten millions)\n\nDigit3:7 (millions)\n\nDigit4:6 (hundred thousands)\n\nDigit5:2 (ten thousands)\n\nDigit6:2 (thousands)\n\nDigit7:7 (hundreds)\n\nDigit8:2 (tens)\n\nDigit9:9 (ones)\n\nSo when adding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the ones (digit9):\n\n7 (first) +9 (second)=16 → 6, carryover1\n\nDigit8 (tens):9 +2=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1\n\nDigit7 (hundreds):9 +7=16 +1=17 →7, carryover1\n\nDigit6 (thousands):5 +2=7 +1=8 →8, carryover0\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):2 +2=4 →4, carryover0\n\nDigit4 (hundred thousands):5 +6=11 →1, carryover1\n\nDigit3 (millions):1 +7=8 +1=9 →9, carryover0\n\nDigit2 (ten millions):9 +9=18 →8, carryover1\n\nDigit1 (hundred millions):5 +3=8 +1 (carryover)=9 →9, no carryover.\n\nSo the digits from highest to lowest (hundred millions down to ones) are:\n\n9 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),9 (millions),1 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),7 (hundreds),2 (tens),6 (ones).\n\nTherefore the number is 989,148,726.\n\nWait, but earlier when I thought of 591 million plus 397 million is 988 million, and adding the remaining parts gives 525,997 + 622,729 = 1,148,726. So total is 591,525,997 + 397,622,729 = 988,000,000 + 1,148,726 = 989,148,726. Yes, that matches. So the final answer should be 989,148,726.\n\nI think that's correct. Let me just verify once again with another method. Maybe adding in parts.\n\nFirst, add the millions parts:\n\n591,525,997 can be broken into 591,000,000 + 525,997.\n\n397,622,729 is 397,000,000 + 622,729.\n\nAdding the millions: 591,000,000 + 397,000,000 = 988,000,000.\n\nAdding the smaller parts: 525,997 + 622,729.\n\nLet's add those:\n\n525,997 + 622,729.\n\nStart with 525,000 + 622,000 = 1,147,000.\n\nThen add 997 +729: 997+700=1,697 +29=1,726.\n\nSo total of smaller parts: 1,147,000 +1,726 = 1,148,726.\n\nAdding to the 988,000,000 gives 989,148,726. Yep, matches. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore the answer is 989,148,726.\n\nWait, but in the digit-by-digit addition earlier, the digits were 9 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),9 (millions),1 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),7 (hundreds),2 (tens),6 (ones). So written as 989,148,726. Exactly. So that's correct.\n\nI think that's right. I don't see any mistakes now.\n</think>", '']  3%|3         | 17/500 [23:31<12:16:28, 91.49s/it]
