final_output:  ["1,547,361,228?\n\nWait, let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nFirst, add 800,000,000 + 700,000,000 = 1,500,000,000.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 33,808,999 + 13,552,229.\n\n33,808,999 +10,000,000 is 43,808,999. Then add 3,552,229: 43,808,999 +3,552,229 = 47,361,228.\n\nAdding that to the 1.5 billion: 1,500,000,000 +47,361,228 =1,547,361,228. Okay, so that matches. So the final sum is 1,547,361,228. Let me check once more with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like addition step by step:\n\n833,808,999\n\n+713,552,229\n\nStart adding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nDigit positions (from right, starting at 1):\n\n1 (ones): 9 +9 =18 → 8, carry 1\n\n2 (tens):9 +2=11 +1=12 →2, carry1\n\n3 (hundreds):9+2=11 +1=12 →2, carry1\n\n4 (thousands):8+2=10 +1=11 →1, carry1\n\n5 (ten thousands):0+5=5 +1=6 →6, no carry\n\n6 (hundred thousands):8+5=13 →3, carry1\n\n7 (millions):3+3=6 +1=7 →7, no carry\n\n8 (ten millions):8+1=9 →9\n\n9 (hundred millions):3+7=10 →0, carry1\n\n10 (billions):8+7=15 +1=16 →6, carry1\n\n11 (10 billions): carryover1 →1\n\nSo writing all digits from right to left:\n\nPositions 1-11: 8 (1),2(2),2(3),1(4),6(5),3(6),7(7),9(8),0(9),6(10),1(11). So the number is 1 5 4 7 3 6 1 2 2 8? Wait, let me arrange them properly.\n\nWait the digits from highest to lowest place:\n\nThe first digit (leftmost) is the 10 billions place:1\n\nThen billions:5 (since 16 in billions place gives 6, but with carryover 1, so actually, when we had the billions place, 8 (hundred millions?) Wait, maybe I got confused in the numbering.\n\nWait let's recount the positions properly:\n\nLet me write each number with commas for clarity:\n\n833,808,999 is:\n\nDigit positions (from right, place values):\n\n1: 9 (ones)\n\n2:9 (tens)\n\n3:9 (hundreds)\n\n4:8 (thousands)\n\n5:0 (ten thousands)\n\n6:8 (hundred thousands)\n\n7:3 (millions)\n\n8:8 (ten millions)\n\n9:3 (hundred millions)\n\n10:8 (billions)\n\nSimilarl