8+4=12 +1=13. Write3, carryover1.\nPosition9:6+3=9 +1=10. Write0, carryover1. But there are no more digits, so we add the carryover 1 at the beginning.\n\nWait, so the total digits would now be 10 because of the final carryover. Let me track each step properly.\n\nLet me retrace:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones place: 0+7=7. Record 7. Carryover 0.\n\n2. Tens place:5+1=6. Record 6. Carryover 0.\n\n3. Hundreds place:9+2=11. Record 1, carryover 1.\n\n4. Thousands place:3 +7 =10, plus 1 carried over =11. Record 1, carryover1.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:7+9=16, plus 1 carried over =17. Record7, carryover1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:7+2=9, plus 1 carried over =10. Record0, carryover1.\n\n7. Millions place:8+9=17, plus1=18. Record8, carryover1.\n\n8. Ten millions place:8 +4=12, plus1=13. Record3, carryover1.\n\n9. Hundred millions place:6 +3=9, plus1=10. Record0, carryover1.\n\nNow, since we've reached the highest digit (hundred millions), but there's still a carryover of 1. So we need to add a new digit to the left, which is the billions place. So that 1 is added there.\n\nSo putting all together, from right to left (positions 1 to 10):.\n\nDigits recorded in each position (from right to left):.\n\nPosition1:7.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition3:1.\n\nPosition4:1.\n\nPosition5:7.\n\nPosition6:0.\n\nPosition7:8.\n\nPosition8:3.\n\nPosition9:0.\n\nPosition10:1 (the final carryover).\n\nTherefore, writing the number from left to right, the digits are:.\n\n1 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands?), Wait, maybe I need to list them properly.\n\nWait, the positions were numbered from right (ones) as position1. So position10 is the leftmost digit here, which is the billions place.\n\nSo the number would be:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:0 (from position9's recorded 0 plus carryover?).\n\nWait, perhaps it's better to list the digits in order:.\n\nStarting from the highest place (billions):.\n\n1 (from the final carryover