sition1 (ones):8.\n\nPosition2 (tens):1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):9.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):2.\n\nPosition7 (millions):1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):0.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):9.\n\nSo adding each position:.\n\nStarting from position1:.\n\n1: 2 +8=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition2:7 +1 +1 (carry)=9. Write 9, carry 0.\n\nPosition3:1 +9 +0=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nPosition4:7 (first) +9 (second)=16, plus carryover1 makes 17. So write7, carryover1.\n\nPosition5:2 +0 +1=3. Write3, carry 0.\n\nPosition6:7 +2=9. Write9, carry0.\n\nPosition7:3 +1=4. Write4, carry0.\n\nPosition8:9 (first) +0 (second)=9. Write9, carry0.\n\nPosition9:6 +9=15. So here, since it's the highest position, we need to write 15. But since that's two digits, the total becomes 15 followed by the previous digits.\n\nWait, so putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nPositions 1-9:.\n\nThe carryover from position9 (15) would add another digit? Wait, position9 is the hundred millions place. Adding 6 (from first number) and9 (second) gives 15, so that's 5 in the hundred millions place and carryover 1 to a new billion place.\n\nAh, right! I almost forgot that adding the hundred millions (6+9=15) would require a new digit in the billions place. So the total sum will have an extra digit.\n\nLet me retrace:.\n\nStarting from position1 (ones):.\n\nAfter processing all positions up to position9 (hundred millions):.\n\nPosition9 sum:6+9=15. So we write down 5 in the hundred millions place and carryover 1 to the billions place (position10).\n\nTherefore, the total sum is 1 (carryover) followed by the digits from the previous positions.\n\nLet me write all digits step by step:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position1 to position10):.\n\nPosition1: 0.\n\nPosition2:9.\n\nPosition3:0.\n\nPosition4:7.\n\nPosition5:3.\n\nPosition6:9.\n\nPosition7:4.\n\nPosition8:9.\n\nPosition9:5.\n\nPosition10:1 (the carried ove