lace, after adding the carry-over, is 1 (since there were no digits there except the carry). So the final digits would be 1 (billion) 0 (hundred millions), then the rest as computed.\n\nPutting it all together, let me write each step again more carefully, perhaps in a table:.\n\nLet me write the numbers aligned properly:.\n\n          7 3 5 0 2 0 9 1 5.\n        + 3 0 8 4 3 3 3 1 1.\n        ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 5 +1 =6.\n\nTens:1 +1=2.\n\nHundreds:9+3=12 → write 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:0+3=3 +1=4.\n\nTen-thousands:2+3=5.\n\nHundred-thousands:0+4=4.\n\nMillions:5+8=13 → write 3, carryover 1.\n\nTen-millions:3+0=3 +1=4 (Wait, the ten millions place for first number is 3, second is 0?).\n\nWait, let me check the digits again step by step for each position. Maybe I got confused in the millions place.\n\nWait, let me list each digit position by position:.\n\nLet me write each number digit by digit with their place values:.\n\nFirst number: 735,020,915.\n\nBreaking down each digit from right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\nPosition (from right): 1 (ones) to 9 (hundred millions).\n\nDigit positions:.\n\n1: 5 (ones).\n\n2:1 (tens).\n\n3:9 (hundreds).\n\n4:0 (thousands).\n\n5:2 (ten thousands).\n\n6:0 (hundred thousands).\n\n7:5 (millions).\n\n8:3 (ten millions).\n\n9:7 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 308,433,311.\n\nDigits from right to left:.\n\n1:1 (ones).\n\n2:1 (tens).\n\n3:3 (hundreds).\n\n4:3 (thousands).\n\n5:3 (ten thousands).\n\n6:4 (hundred thousands).\n\n7:8 (millions).\n\n8:0 (ten millions).\n\n9:3 (hundred millions).\n\nNow, adding each column starting from position 1 (ones):.\n\nPosition 1: 5 +1 =6.\n\nPosition 2:1 +1=2.\n\nPosition3:9 +3=12 → 2, carryover 1.\n\nPosition4:0 +3 =3 +1 (carry) =4.\n\nPosition5:2 +3=5.\n\nPosition6:0 +4=4.\n\nPosition7:5 (millions from first) +8 (millions from second) =13 → 3, carryover1.\n\nPosition8:3 (ten millions from first) +0 (ten millions from second) 