s place:6 +7 =13. Write 3, carry 1.\n\n9. Hundred millions place:8 +2 +1 =11. Write 1, carry over 1.\n\n10. The final carryover 1 becomes the next digit (billions place).\n\nThus, combining all digits: 1 (billions) 1 (hundred millions) 3 (ten millions) 6 (millions) 1 (hundred thousands) 6 (ten thousands) 4 (thousands) 5 (hundreds) 7 (tens) 7 (ones). So the sum is 1,136,164,577.\n\nI need to present this in the template, following the user's example. So in the Reasoning section, list each step with the digit places, their sums, and carryovers. Then the answer at the end.\n</think>", '']
