ers have only 9 digits, the first has 9 (hundred millions), but the carryover from the hundred millions addition is 1, so that becomes a new digit in the billions place. So the total here would be 1 (carryover) → so the final digit is 1 followed by the rest?.\n\nWait, let me go through again step by step to make sure I didn't mix up the positions.\n\nLet me list each digit from right to left (starting at ones):.\n\nFirst number: 981574076.\n\nDigits (right to left):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):6.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):7.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):0.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):4.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):7.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5.\n\nPosition7 (millions):1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):8.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):9.\n\nSecond number:769507636.\n\nDigits (right to left):.\n\nPosition1:6.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition3:6.\n\nPosition4:7.\n\nPosition5:0.\n\nPosition6:5.\n\nPosition7:9.\n\nPosition8:6.\n\nPosition9:7.\n\nSo adding each position:.\n\nPosition1:6+6=12 → 2, carryover1.\n\nPosition2:7+3=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nPosition3:0+6=6 +1=7 →7, no carryover.\n\nPosition4:4+7=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nPosition5:7+0=7 +1=8 →8, no carryover.\n\nPosition6:5+5=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nPosition7:1+9=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nPosition8:8+6=14 +1=15 →5, carryover1.\n\nPosition9:9+7=16 +1=17 →7, carryover1.\n\nNow, after the hundred millions place (position9), we have a carryover of 1. Since there are no more digits beyond that, this carryover becomes a new digit at the billions place (position10). So the total sum will have a 1 in the billions place followed by the previous digits.\n\nPutting all together from last to first (since we built from right to left):.\n\nThe digits from position1 to position10 are:.\n\nPosition1:2.\n\nPosition2:1.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition4:1.\n\nPosition5:8.\n\nPosition6:0.\n\nPosition7:1.\n\nPosition8:5.\n\nPosition9:7.\n\nPosition10:1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
