ten millions place is actually 4 (since 140,712,564 has the digits as 1 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 0 (millions), etc.). So that's where the mistake was. So the correct answer is 842,778,196. \n\nSo the correct reasoning should reflect that. Let me structure it properly now.\n</think>", '']
