ndred thousands)\n\n7:9 (millions)\n\n8:6 (ten millions)\n\n9:4 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number:720,402,451\n\nDigits from right:\n\n1:1 (ones)\n\n2:5 (tens)\n\n3:4 (hundreds)\n\n4:2 (thousands)\n\n5:0 (ten thousands)\n\n6:4 (hundred thousands)\n\n7:0 (millions)\n\n8:2 (ten millions)\n\n9:7 (hundred millions)\n\nNow, adding column by column:\n\n1. Ones: 2 +1 =3. Write 3.\n\n2. Tens:3 +5=8. Write 8.\n\n3. Hundreds:2 +4=6. Write 6.\n\n4. Thousands:0 +2=2. Write 2.\n\n5. Ten thousands:8 +0=8. Write 8.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:1 +4=5. Write 5.\n\n7. Millions:9 +0=9. Write 9.\n\n8. Ten millions:6 +2=8. Write 8.\n\n9. Hundred millions:4 +7=11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\nThen, since there's a carryover from the hundred millions, we have an additional 1 in the billions place. So the total is 1 (billions) 1 (hundred millions) followed by the rest.\n\nPutting it all together:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:8\n\nMillions:9\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:2\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:3\n\nWait, that gives 1,189,582,683? Let me see:\n\nBreaking down the sum digit by digit:\n\nBillions place:1\n\nHundred millions:1 → so first three digits: 118?\n\nWait, let's list each digit position:\n\nPosition 9 (billions):1\n\nPosition8 (hundred millions):1\n\nPosition7 (ten millions):8\n\nPosition6 (millions):9\n\nPosition5 (hundred thousands):5\n\nPosition4 (ten thousands):8\n\nPosition3 (thousands):2\n\nPosition2 (hundreds):6\n\nPosition1 (tens):8\n\nPosition0 (ones):3\n\nWait, so the number is:\n\n1 (billions), 1 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),9 (millions),5 (hundred thousands),8 (ten thousands),2 (thousands),6 (hundreds),8 (tens),3 (ones). So that's 1,189,582,683.\n\nWait, but let's check with another method. Let me add the numbers using another approach:\n\n469,180,232 +720,402,451.\n\nAdding 469 million to 720 million: that's 1,189 million.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 180,232 +402,451 = 582,683.\n\nSo total is 1,189,582,683. Yes, that matches. So my initial calculation was correct. The previous confusion was because I might have miscounted the places earlier, but breaking it down step by step confirms the answer is correct. So the final answer is 1,189,582,683.\n\n</think>", ''] 21%|##        | 104/500 [2:27:45<12:01:41, 109.35s/it]
