red millions, so that carried-over 1 becomes a 1 in the billions place.\n\nPutting it all together: the billions place is 1, then 0 in hundred millions, 6 in ten millions, 8 in millions, 5 in hundred thousands, 6 in ten thousands, 7 in thousands, 9 in hundreds, 3 in tens, and 9 in ones. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits.\n\nWait a second, maybe I should write each step more carefully. Let me do the addition step by step:.\n\nLet me align the numbers:.\n\n      706,600,485.\n    + 370,967,454.\n    ----------------.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 5 + 4 = 9.\n\nTens: 8 + 5 = 13 (carry 1).\n\nHundreds: 4 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 9.\n\nThousands: 0 +7 =7.\n\nTen thousands: 0 +6 =6.\n\nHundred thousands: 6 +9 =15 (carry 1).\n\nMillions: 0 +7 +1 =8.\n\nTen millions: 6 +0 =6.\n\nHundred millions: 7 +3 =10 (carry 1).\n\nBillions: 1 (from carry) since there are no higher digits.\n\nSo putting all the digits together:.\n\nBillions: 1.\n\nHundred millions: 0 (since 7+3=10, the 0 stays here, and the 1 is carried over).\n\nTen millions: 6.\n\nMillions:8.\n\nHundred thousands:5.\n\nTen thousands:6.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nTens:3.\n\nOnes:9</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
