, carryover1.\n\nDigit3 (hundreds):2 +4=6 +1=7, no carryover.\n\nDigit4 (thousands):3 +1=4. No carryover.\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):5 +5=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nDigit6 (hundred thousands):6 +7=13 +1=14 →4, carryover1.\n\nDigit7 (millions):5 +1=6 +1=7, no carryover.\n\nDigit8 (ten millions):3 +5=8.\n\nDigit9 (hundred millions):3 +1=4.\n\nPutting all the digits together from digit1 to digit9:.\n\nDigits:.\n\n1 (ones):0.\n\n2 (tens):4.\n\n3 (hundreds):7.\n\n4 (thousands):4.\n\n5 (ten thousands):0.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):4.\n\n7 (millions):7.\n\n8 (ten millions):8.\n\n9 (hundred millions):4.\n\nSo combining all digits: 4 (hundred millions),8 (ten millions),7 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),4 (hundreds?), wait no, let me see:.\n\nWait the digits are from digit9 (leftmost) to digit1 (rightmost):.\n\nSo the final number is:.\n\nDigit9:4, Digit8:8, Digit7:7, Digit6:4, Digit5:0, Digit4:4, Digit3:7, Digit2:4, Digit1:0.\n\nWait arranging them in order:.\n\nHundred millions:4,.\n\nTen millions:8,.\n\nMillions:7,.\n\nHundred thousands:4,.\n\nTen thousands:0,.\n\nThousands:4,.\n\nHundreds:7,.\n\nTens:4,.\n\nOnes:0</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
