rryover1.\n\nHundreds:8 +4 =12, plus1 →13. Write3, carryover1.\n\nThousands:2 +4 =6, plus1 →7. Write7, no carry.\n\nTen thousands:1 +2 =3. Write3.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +9 =14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nMillions:7 (first) +2 (second) =9, plus carryover1 →10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:0 (first) +2 (second) =2, plus carryover1 →3. Write3.\n\nHundred millions:2 +3 =5. Write5.\n\nWait wait, that can't be. Wait the hundred millions place: first number has 2, second has 3. So 2+3=5. But in the ten millions place, first number has 0 and second has 2, plus the carryover 1 from millions, so 0+2+1=3. .\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum would be:.\n\nStarting from the right, digits are:.\n\nOnes:2.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:3.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nMillions:0.\n\nTen millions:3.\n\nHundred millions:5.\n\nWait that would give the number 530,343,732? Wait let me write the digits in order:.\n\nHundred millions:5.\n\nTen millions:3.\n\nMillions:0.\n\nHundred thousands:3?.\n\nWait I think I messed up the place values. Let me list each digit position step by step.\n\nLet me structure it properly:.\n\nEach digit from right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 5 +7 =12 → 2, carry1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):5 +9 +1 =15 →5, carry1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):8 +4 +1 =13 →3, carry1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):2 +4 +0 =6 + carry1 →7, carry0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):1 +2 =3 →3, carry0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5 +9 =14 →4, carry1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):7 +2 +1 (carry) =10 →0, carry1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):0 +2 +1 (carry) =3 →3, carry0.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):2 +3 =5 →5, carry0.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:.\n\n2 (ones),5 (tens),3 (hundreds),7 (thousands),3 (ten thousands),4 (hundred thousands),0 (millions),3 (ten millions),5 (hundred millions).\n\nSo writing the number from highest to lowest place:.\n\nHundred millions (5), ten millions (3), millions (0), hundred thousands (4?), wait w