 1 equals 2. So millions place is 2, no carryover here.\n\nMoving to the ten millions place. The first number has a 9 and the second has a 9. 9 + 9 is 18. That's a big number. So the ten millions place will be 8, and we carry over 1 to the hundred millions place.\n\nFinally, the hundred millions place. The first number has a 2 and the second has a 6. Adding them gives 8, plus the carried over 1 makes 9. So the hundred millions place is 9</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
