Position4 (Thousands):4+2=6.\n\nPosition5 (Ten thousands):1+6=7.\n\nPosition6 (Hundred thousands):6+2=8.\n\nPosition7 (Millions):6 (from first's millions) +7 (second's millions)=13 → write 3, carryover 1.\n\nPosition8 (Ten millions): first's ten millions is 2, second's ten millions is5 →2+5=7 plus carryover 1 → total 8. So ten millions digit is8, no carryover.\n\nPosition9 (Hundred millions):5+2=7.\n\nSo the digits are:.\n\nPosition9:7.\n\nPosition8:8.\n\nPosition7:3.\n\nPosition6:8.\n\nPosition5:7.\n\nPosition4:6.\n\nPosition3:2.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition1:2.\n\nSo constructing the number from highest to lowest:.\n\nHundred millions:7,.\n\nTen millions:8,.\n\nMillions:3,.\n\nHundred thousands:8,.\n\nTen thousands:7,.\n\nThousands:6,.\n\nHundreds:2,.\n\nTens:3,.\n\nOnes:2</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
