000 + 6,000 + 700 + 40 +1.\n\nAdding term by term:\n\n600M +900M =1,500,000,000.\n\n80M +70M =150,000,000.\n\n2M +8M=10,000,000.\n\n900k +600k=1,500,000.\n\n60k +90k=150,000.\n\n1k +6k=7,000.\n\n700+700=1,400.\n\n50+40=90.\n\n6+1=7.\n\nNow adding all these together:\n\nStart with 1,500,000,000 +150,000,000 =1,650,000,000.\n\nPlus 10,000,000 →1,660,000,000.\n\nPlus 1,500,000 →1,661,500,000.\n\nPlus 150,000 →1,661,650,000.\n\nPlus 7,000 →1,661,657,000.\n\nPlus 1,400 →1,661,658,400.\n\nPlus 90 →1,661,658,490.\n\nPlus 7 →1,661,658,497.\n\nYes, that matches the previous result. So the sum is indeed 1,661,658,497.\n\nSo the answer should be 1,661,658,497. Let me check once more with a calculator approach.\n\nAlternatively, adding digit by digit again to confirm:\n\n682,961,756\n\n+978,696,741\n\nAdding units:6+1=7.\n\nTens:5+4=9.\n\nHundreds:7+7=14 (4, carryover1).\n\nThousands:1+6=7 +1=8.\n\nTen thousands:6+9=15 (5, carryover1).\n\nHundred thousands:9+6=15 +1=16 (6, carryover1).\n\nMillions:2+8=10 +1=11 (1, carryover1).\n\nTen millions:8+7=15 +1=16 (6, carryover1).\n\nHundred millions:6+9=15 +1=16 (6, carryover1).\n\nBillions: carryover1.\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 7,9,4,8,5,6,1,6,6,1.\n\nSo the number is 1,661,658,497. Yes, that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 1,661,658,497.\n\n</think>", '']
