ver 1.\n\nThen the final carryover 1 becomes the next digit (billions place).\n\nSo the digits from right to left would be:\n\n5,9,0,6,4,6,4,0,0,1. Wait, no. Let me write each position's result:\n\nAfter all steps:\n\nPosition1:5\n\nPosition2:9\n\nPosition3:0 (with carry 1)\n\nPosition4:6\n\nPosition5:4 (carry 1)\n\nPosition6:6\n\nPosition7:4\n\nPosition8:0 (carry1)\n\nPosition9:0 (since 5+4+1=10, so 0 and carry1)\n\nPosition10:1 (from the carryover)\n\nSo arranging all digits from position1 (ones) to position10 (billions):\n\nPositions:\n\n10:1\n\n9:0\n\n8:0\n\n7:4\n\n6:6\n\n5:4\n\n4:6\n\n3:0\n\n2:9\n\n1:5\n\nWait, no, that can't be right. Wait, positions are numbered from right (1) to left (10). So the final number is:\n\nBillions (position10):1\n\nHundred millions (position9):0\n\nTen millions (position8):0\n\nMillions (position7):4\n\nHundred thousands (position6):6\n\nTen thousands (position5):4\n\nThousands (position4):6\n\nHundreds (position3):0\n\nTens (position2):9\n\nOnes (position1):5\n\nSo the number is 1,004,646,095. Which matches the earlier result. So my initial calculation was correct. The confusion was in the position8 step where I had to carry over, leading to the hundred millions place becoming 0 with another carryover.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is indeed 1,004,646,095. I should make sure that in the reasoning, each digit place is correctly noted. Let me structure the reasoning step by step as per the template.\n\nThe problem is to add 593,495,461 and 411,150,634.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):\n\n1. Ones place: 1 + 4 = 5.\n\n2. Tens place: 6 + 3 = 9.\n\n3. Hundreds place: 4 + 6 = 10. Write down 0, carry over 1.\n\n4. Thousands place: 5 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 6.\n\n5. Ten thousands place: 9 + 5 = 14. Write down 4, carry over 1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place: 4 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 6.\n\n7. Millions place: 3 + 1 = 4.\n\n8. Ten millions place: 9 + 1 = 10. Write down 0, carry over 1.\n\n9. Hundred millions place: 5 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 