xth digit).\nThousands:7 (seventh digit).\nHundreds:9 (eighth digit).\nTens:1 (ninth digit).\nOnes: ?.\n\nWait, I'm getting mixed up. Let's write it properly. Let's separate each digit:.\n\nThe number 691,814,791 is:.\n\nDigit positions (from right to left):.\n\n1 (ones): 1.\n\n2 (tens):9.\n\n3 (hundreds):7.\n\n4 (thousands):4.\n\n5 (ten thousands):1.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):8.\n\n7 (millions):1.\n\n8 (ten millions):9.\n\n9 (hundred millions):6.\n\nYes, that's correct. So the first number's digits are:.\n\nPositions 1-9 (right to left):.\n\n1:1, 2:9, 3:7, 4:4, 5:1, 6:8, 7:1, 8:9, 9:6.\n\nSecond number: 927,053,039.\n\nBreaking it down similarly:.\n\nDigit positions (right to left):.\n\n1 (ones):9.\n\n2 (tens):3.\n\n3 (hundreds):0.\n\n4 (thousands):3.\n\n5 (ten thousands):5.\n\n6 (hundred thousands):0.\n\n7 (millions):7.\n\n8 (ten millions):2.\n\n9 (hundred millions):9.\n\nSo now adding each position with carries.\n\nLet me go step by step:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):.\n\nNumber1:1, Number2:9 → 1+9=10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition2 (tens):.\n\nNumber1:9, Number2:3 →9+3=12 +1=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):.\n\nNumber1:7, Number2:0 →7+0=7 +1=8. Write 8, carryover 0.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):.\n\nNumber1:4, Number2:3 →4+3=7 +0=7. Write 7, carryover 0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):.\n\nNumber1:1, Number2:5 →1+5=6 +0=6. Write 6, carryover 0.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\n\nNumber1:8, Number2:0 →8+0=8 +0=8. Write 8, carryover 0.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\nNumber1:1, Number2:7 →1+7=8 +0=8. Write 8, carryover 0.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\nNumber1:9, Number2:2 →9+2=11 +0=11. Wait, here, 9+2 is 11. So write 1 and carryover 1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\nNumber1:6, Number2:9 →6+9=15 +1 (carryover) =16. So write 6 and carryover 1.\n\nBut wait, after the hundred millions place, which is the 9th digit, there's an additional carryover of 1. Since there are no more digits, we need to add a new digit at the billions place (10th position). So the final digit is 1, followed by the previous digits.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the last carryover:.\n\nThe result would be 1 (from the carryover) followed by the digits we've written from position9 to position1:.\n\nWait, let me list all the digits:.\n\nStarting from the highest place (billions place, which is the 10th digit now because of the carryover):.\n\n1 (carryover).\n\nThen position9 (hundred millions) was 6 (since 15+1=16 → 6 with carryover 1). Wait, no:.\n\nWait, let me retrace the steps:.\n\nAfter adding position9 (hundred millions):.\n\nNumber1's hundred millions digit is 6, Number2's is 9. So 6+9 =15. Then add the carryover from the previous (position8):.\n\nWait, position8: ten millions place.\n\nWait, when adding position8 (ten millions):.\n\nNumber1 has 9, Number2 has 2. So 9+2=11. So we write down 1 in that position and carryover 1 to the next (hundred millions place).\n\nSo when we get to the hundred millions place (position9):.\n\n6 (from number1) +9 (number2) + the carryover 1 from position8 → total 16. So 6 in hundred millions, carryover 1 to the next (billions place).\n\nSince there are no more digits, the carryover 1 becomes the billions place (position10). .\n\nSo the digits from position10 down to position1 are:.\n\nPosition10:1.\n\nPosition9:6.\n\nPosition8:1 (from the ten millions place calculation, since 9+2=11, so we wrote 1 there?).\n\nWait, let me re-express each position's result:.\n\nLet me tabulate each step with the result and carryover:.\n\n1. Position 1 (ones): 1+9=10 → 0, carry 1.\n\nResult so far: 0 (ones).\n\nCarry:1.\n\n2. Position 2 (tens):9+3=12 +1=13 →3, carry1.\n\nResult: 3 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nCarry:1.\n\n3. Position3 (hundreds):7+0=7 +1=8 →8, carry0.\n\nResult:8 (hundreds),3 (tens),0.\n\nCarry:0.\n\n4. Position4 (thousands):4+3=7 →7, carry0.\n\nResult:7 (thousands),8,3,0.\n\nCarry:0.\n\n5. Position5 (ten thousands):1+5=6 →6, carry0.\n\nResult:6 (ten thousands),7,8,3,0.\n\nCarry:0.\n\n6. Position6 (hundred thousands):8+0=8 →8, carry0.\n\nResult:8 (hundred thous),6,7,8,3,0.\n\nCarry:0.\n\n7. Position7 (millions):1+7=8 →8, carry0.\n\nResult:8 (millions),8,6,7,8,3,0.\n\nCarry:0.\n\n8. Position8 (ten millions):9+2=11 →1, carry1.\n\nResult:1 (ten millions),8,8,6,7,8,3,0.\n\nCarry:1.\n\n9. Position9 (hundred millions):6+9=15 +1(carry)=16 →6, carry1.\n\nResult:6 (hundred millions),1,8,8,6,7,8,3,0.\n\nCarry:1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 1 after the hundred millions place, we add a new digit (billions place):.\n\n10. Position10 (billions): carryover 1 →1.\n\nSo the final digits from highest to lowest (billions to ones):.\n\n1 (billions), 6 (hundred millions),1 (ten millions),8 (millions),8 (hundred thousands),6 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),8 (hundreds),3 (tens),0 (ones).\n\nWait, let me check the sequence again:.\n\nThe result digits from position10 down:.\n\nPosition10:1.\n\nPosition9:6.\n\nPosition8:1.\n\nPosition7:8.\n\nPosition6:8.\n\nPosition5:6.\n\nPosition4:7.\n\nPosition3:8.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition1:0.\n\nWait, arranging them in order from billions down to ones:.\n\nBillions (pos10):1.\n\nHundred millions (pos9):6.\n\nTen millions (pos8):1.\n\nMillions (pos7):8.\n\nHundred thousands (pos6):8.\n\nTen thousands (pos5):6.\n\nThousands (pos4):7.\n\nHundreds (pos3):8.\n\nTens (pos2):3.\n\nOnes (pos1):0</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
