es: 1+1=2.\n\nTens:7+7=14, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds:2+9=11 +1=12, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:1+9=10 +1=11, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands:9 (from first number) +0 (second)=9+1=10? Wait, the ten thousands place: first number's digit is the 5th from the right. Let me see:.\n\nBreaking down 390,791,271:.\n\nDigits: 3 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 1 (ones).\n\nSimilarly, 647,909,971:.\n\n6 (hundred millions),4 (ten millions),7 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),9 (hundreds),7 (tens),1 (ones).\n\nSo when adding the ten thousands place: first number has 9, second has 0. So 9+0=9 plus carryover 1 makes 10. So we write 0 and carryover 1.\n\nThen hundred thousands place: first is 7, second is9. 7+9=16, plus carryover 1 is 17. Wait, hold on, I might have messed up earlier steps. Let me redo this step by step properly.\n\nLet me align them properly:.\n\n          3 9 0 7 9 1 2 7 1.\n\n        + 6 4 7 9 0 9 9 7 1.\n\n        -------------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\nOnes place: 1 + 1 = 2. Write 2.\n\nTens place: 7 + 7 = 14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 9 = 11, plus 1 = 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nThousands place: 1 + 9 = 10, plus 1 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place: 9 (from first number) + 0 (second number) =9 + 1 (carryover) = 10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nHundred thousands place: 7 (first) +9 (second) =16, plus 1 =17. Write 7, carryover 1.\n\nMillions place: 0 (first) +7 (second) =7 +1 =8. Write 8, no carryover.\n\nTen millions place:9 (first) +4 (second) =13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nHundred millions place:3 (first) +6 (second) =9, plus 1 carried over =10. So write 0 and carryover 1. But since there's no higher place, that 1 is added as a new digit at the beginning.\n\nWait, so putting it all together, the sum would be:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are:.\n\nOnes:2.\n\nT