:0,\n\nMillions (Position7):6,\n\nHundred thousands (Position6):8,\n\nTen thousands (Position5):8,\n\nThousands (Position4):9,\n\nHundreds (Position3):9,\n\nTens (Position2):8,\n\nOnes (Position1):8.\n\nSo writing that out:\n\n8 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 8 (ones).\n\nPutting commas in: 806,889,988? Wait, let's see:\n\nBreaking down the digits:\n\nStarting from the highest:\n\n8 (hundred millions),\n\n0 (ten millions),\n\n6 (millions),\n\n8 (hundred thousands),\n\n8 (ten thousands),\n\n9 (thousands),\n\n9 (hundreds),\n\n8 (tens),\n\n8 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 806,889,988.\n\nWait, but let me confirm this again because when I first thought I had 743 million, but now it's 806 million. Hmm, must have made a mistake earlier.\n\nWait let me recalculate the hundred millions place:\n\nPosition9: 4 (from first number) +3 (from second) +1 (carry from Position8?) Wait, no.\n\nWait the carryover from the ten millions place (Position8) is 1, right? Let me retrace:\n\nPosition8 (Ten millions place):\n\nDigits from each number: first number has 9, second has 1. So 9 +1 =10. So we write 0 and carryover 1 to the next (hundred millions) place.\n\nThen the hundred millions place is 4 (first) +3 (second) + that 1 carried over, which is 8. So that part is correct.\n\nSo the total is 806,889,988. Let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers numerically:\n\n429,983,541\n\n+313,906,447\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 429,983,541 + 300,000,000 = 729,983,541\n\nThen add 13,906,447:\n\n729,983,541 + 13,906,447\n\n729,983,541 +10,000,000 =739,983,541\n\nThen add 3,906,447:\n\n739,983,541 +3,906,447 = ?\n\nAdding 3,000,000: 742,983,541\n\nThen 906,447:\n\n742,983,541 +906,447 = ?\n\n742,983,541 +900,000 = 743,883,541\n\nThen +6,447: 743,883,541 +6,447 =743,889,988\n\nWait a second, now this gives a different result: 743,889,988.\n\nBut earlier step-by-digit addition gave 806,889,988. There's a discrepancy here. Which is correct?\n\nHmm, I must have messed up the digit positions in the first method. Let me check the second approach again.\n\nWait 429,983,541 + 313,906,447.\n\nLet me do it digit by digit again carefully.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 1 +7=8.\n\nTens:4+4=8.\n\nHundreds:5+4=9.\n\nThousands:3 +6=9.\n\nTen thousands:8 +0=8.\n\nHundred thousands:9 +9=18 (write 8, carry 1).\n\nMillions:2 +3 +1=6.\n\nTen millions:9 +1=10 (write 0, carry 1).\n\nHundred millions:4 +3 +1=8.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nHundred millions:8,\n\nTen millions:0,\n\nMillions:6,\n\nHundred thousands:8,\n\nTen thousands:8,\n\nThousands:9,\n\nHundreds:9,\n\nTens:8,\n\nOnes:8.\n\nSo that's 806,889,988. But when adding the second way, breaking down the numbers, I got 743,889,988. Which is conflicting. Where is the mistake?\n\nAh! Wait, in the second method, when I added 429,983,541 +313,906,447:\n\nLet me compute this properly with standard addition:\n\n429,983,541\n\n+313,906,447\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1+7=8\n\n4+4=8\n\n5+4=9\n\n3+6=9\n\n8+0=8\n\n9+9=18 (carry 1)\n\n2+3+1=6\n\n9+1=10 (carry 1)\n\n4+3+1=8.\n\nSo that gives 806,889,988. Therefore the second method's earlier breakdown was wrong.\n\nWait why? Let's check the second method again:\n\nFirst step: 429,983,541 +300,000,000 = 729,983,541. Correct.\n\nThen adding 13,906,447 to that:\n\n729,983,541 +13,906,447.\n\nLet me add 10,000,000 first: 729,983,541 +10,000,000 = 739,983,541.\n\nThen add remaining 3,906,447:\n\n739,983,541 +3,906,447.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n739,983,541 +3,000,000 =742,983,541\n\nThen add 906,447: 742,983,541 +906,447.\n\n742,983,541 + 900,000 = 743,883,541.\n\nAdding 6,447: 743,883,541 +6,447 =743,889,988.\n\nWait, so why the discrepancy?\n\nAh! Because in the second method, I added 313,906,447 as 300,000,000 +13,906,447, which is correct. But the problem is that the first number is 429,983,541. So when adding 429,983,541 + 313,906,447:\n\nWait 429,983,541 + 313,906,447 = ?\n\nLet me compute this using another way:\n\n429,983,541\n\n+313,906,447\n\n= (400,000,000 +29,983,541) + (300,000,000 +13,906,447)\n\n= 700,000,000 + (29,983,541 +13,906,447)\n\n29,983,541 +13,906,447:\n\n29,983,541 +10,000,000 =39,983,541\n\n+3,906,447 → 39,983,541 +3,906,447 =43,890,  (Wait let's do it properly):\n\n29,983,541\n\n+13,906,447\n\nAdding:\n\nOnes:1+7=8\n\nTens:4+4=8\n\nHundreds:5+6=11 (carry 1)\n\nThousands:3+4 +1=8\n\nTen thousands:8+0=8\n\nHundred thousands:9+3=12 (carry1)\n\nMillions:9+1 +1=11 (carry1)\n\nTen millions:2+0 +1=3\n\nSo total is 43,890,  (Wait, let's see:\n\nWait 29,983,541 +13,906,447:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n1+7=8\n\n4+4=8\n\n5+6=11 → 1, carryover1\n\n3+4=7 +1=8\n\n8+0=8\n\n9 (hundred thousands) +3 (hundred thousands)=12 → 2 carryover1\n\n9 (millions) +1 (million)=10 +1 (carry)=11 → 1 carryover1\n\n2 (ten millions) +0 +1=3.\n\nSo the total would be 43,890, (wait, let's see the digits:\n\nTen millions place:3 (from 29,983,541's ten millions is 2, but with the carryover?)\n\nWait, maybe better to write it out:\n\n29,983,541\n\n+13,906,447\n\n= ?\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:1+7=8\n\nTens:4+4=8\n\nHundreds:5+6=11 (write 1, carryover1)\n\nThousands:3+4=7 +1=8\n\nTen thousands:8+0=8\n\nHundred thousands:9+3=12 (write 2, carryover1)\n\nMillions:9+1=10 +1=11 (write1, carryover1)\n\nTen millions:2+0=2 +1=3.\n\nSo the total is 43,890, (wait the millions place: after adding, it's 11, so the millions digit is 1 and carryover1 to ten millions. Wait, let's see:\n\nThe number is:\n\nTen millions place:3 (from 2 (original) +0 + carryover1? Wait, the original ten millions digit for 29,983,541 is 2 (since it's 29 million). The other number is 13,906,447, which has 1 in the ten millions place? Wait, 13,906,447 is 13 million, so the ten millions digit is 1, not 0. Wait I think I made a mistake here.\n\nWait 29,983,541 is 29,983,541 which is 2 (ten millions), 9 (milli