sands).\n6: 0 (millions).\n7: 8 (ten millions).\n8: 2 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, maybe it's easier to add digit by digit starting from the right, keeping track of each place step by step.\n\nLet me list each digit position by position:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nPosition 0 (ones):.\nFirst number: 5.\nSecond number: 0.\nSum: 5 + 0 = 5. Write down 5. Carryover 0.\n\nPosition 1 (tens):.\nFirst number: 8.\nSecond number: 6.\nSum: 8 + 6 = 14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 2 (hundreds):.\nFirst number: 3.\nSecond number: 2.\nSum: 3 + 2 = 5, plus carryover 1 → 6. Write 6, carryover 0.\n\nPosition 3 (thousands):.\nFirst number: 0.\nSecond number: 4.\nSum: 0 +4 =4. Write 4, carryover 0.\n\nPosition 4 (ten thousands):.\nFirst number:7.\nSecond number:4.\nSum:7+4=11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 5 (hundred thousands):.\nFirst number:2.\nSecond number:5.\nSum:2+5=7, plus carryover 1 →8. Write 8, carryover 0.\n\nPosition 6 (millions):.\nFirst number:6.\nSecond number:0.\nSum:6+0=6. Write 6, carryover 0.\n\nPosition 7 (ten millions):.\nFirst number:6.\nSecond number:8.\nSum:6 +8=14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 8 (hundred millions):.\nFirst number:6.\nSecond number:2.\nSum:6+2=8, plus carryover 1 →9. Write 9, no carryover</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
