eft, that 1 becomes another digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right, the digits we wrote down are 0,7,2,2,6,2,3,2,8,7, and then the final carried 1. Wait, let me recount the places to make sure I didn't miscount.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the place values. Let me try again more carefully, writing each step:.\n\nLet me write each number with commas for clarity:.\n\n852,989,335.\n890,722,935.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\n1. Ones place: 5 + 5 = 10 → write 0, carry 1.\n2. Tens: 3 + 3 + 1 =7 → 7, no carry.\n3. Hundreds: 3 + 9 =12 → 2, carry 1.\n4. Thousands: 9 + 2 +1=12 → 2, carry 1.\n5. Ten-thousands: 8 +7 +1=16 →6, carry1.\n6. Hundred-thousands: 9 +2 +1=12 →2, carry1.\n7. Millions: 2 (from first number) +0 (since second number's million digit is 7 in the millions? Wait, let me check the numbers again. Wait, maybe I need to break down each digit properly.\n\nWait, perhaps I should write each number digit by digit to avoid confusion. Let me do that.\n\nFirst number: 852,989,335.\n\nBreaking it down digit by digit from right to left (since we add right to left):.\n\nPositions (starting from 0 for the ones place):.\n\nPosition 0: 5 (ones).\nPosition 1: 3 (tens).\nPosition 2: 3 (hundreds).\nPosition 3: 9 (thousands).\nPosition 4: 8 (ten thousands).\nPosition 5: 2 (hundred thousands).\nPosition 6: 9 (millions).\nPosition 7: 5 (ten millions).\nPosition 8: 8 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 890,722,935.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nPosition 0:5.\nPosition1:3.\nPosition2:9.\nPosition3:2.\nPosition4:2.\nPosition5:7.\nPosition6:0 (since the number is 890,722,935, which is 8 9 0 7 2 2 9 3 5. Wait, let me count properly:.\n\nWait, 890,722,935:.\n\nBreaking down each digit:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nDigit positions:.\n\nPosition 0:5 (ones).\nPosition1:3 (tens).\nPosition2:9 (hundreds).\nPosition3:2 (thousands).\nPosition4:2 (ten thousands).\nPosition5:7 (hundred thousands).\nPosition6:0 (millions).\nPosition7:9 (ten millions).\nPosition8:8 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, let me confirm:.\n\nThe second number is 890,722,935. Let's write it out:.\n\nDigits from left to right:.\n\n8 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 5 (ones). Wait, no:.\n\nWait, the number 890,722,935:.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nFirst digit: 8 (hundred millions place).\nSecond:9 (ten millions).\nThird:0 (millions).\nFourth:7 (hundred thousands).\nFifth:2 (ten thousands).\nSixth:2 (thousands).\nSeventh:9 (hundreds).\nEighth:3 (tens).\nNinth:5 (ones).\n\nWait, so when written as 8 9 0 7 2 2 9 3 5:.\n\nPositions from right (starting at 0):.\n\nPosition 8: 8 (hundred millions).\nPosition7:9 (ten millions).\nPosition6:0 (millions).\nPosition5:7 (hundred thousands).\nPosition4:2 (ten thousands).\nPosition3:2 (thousands).\nPosition2:9 (hundreds).\nPosition1:3 (tens).\nPosition0:5 (ones).\n\nHmm, maybe my initial breakdown was off. Let me clarify:.\n\nFirst number: 852,989,335.\n\nDigits from left to right:.\n\n8 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nSo positions from right (0 to 8):.\n\nPosition 8: 8 (hundred millions).\nPosition7:5 (ten millions).\nPosition6:2 (millions).\nPosition5:9 (hundred thousands).\nPosition4:8 (ten thousands).\nPosition3:9 (thousands).\nPosition2:3 (hundreds).\nPosition1:3 (tens).\nPosition0:5 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 890,722,935.\n\nDigits left to right:.\n\n8 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nSo positions from right (0 to 8):.\n\nPosition8:8 (hundred millions).\nPosition7:9 (ten millions).\nPosition6:0 (millions).\nPosition5:7 (hundred thousands).\nPosition4:2 (ten thousands).\nPosition3:2 (thousands).\nPosition2:9 (hundreds).\nPosition1:3 (tens).\nPosition0:5 (ones).\n\nNow, addin