tions 1 to 10):\n\nPosition 1:6\n\n2:7\n\n3:0\n\n4:6\n\n5:5\n\n6:2\n\n7:2\n\n8:4\n\n9:4\n\n10:1\n\nSo writing the number from highest to lowest place (left to right):\n\n1 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 6 (ones). So the number is 1,442,256,076.\n\nWait, let me confirm with another method. Adding the numbers:\n\n688,406,554 + 753,849,522.\n\nLet's break them into parts:\n\n688,406,554\n\n+753,849,522\n\n= (600,000,000 + 88,406,554) + (700,000,000 + 53,849,522)\n\n= 600M +700M =1,300M\n\nThen 88,406,554 +53,849,522 = ?\n\n88,406,554 +53,849,522:\n\n88,406,554\n\n+53,849,522\n\nAdding:\n\nUnits:\n\n4+2=6\n\n5+2=7\n\n5+5=10 (carry 1)\n\n6+9=15+1=16 (carry1)\n\n0+4=4+1=5\n\n4+8=12 (carry1, digit2)\n\n8+3=11+1=12 (carry1, digit2)\n\n8+5=13+1=14 (carry1, digit4)\n\nSo 142,256,076?\n\nWait, 88,406,554 +53,849,522:\n\nLet me compute:\n\n88,406,554\n\n+53,849,522\n\nAdding:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n4+2=6\n\n5+2=7\n\n5+5=10 (0, carry1)\n\n6+9=15 +1=16 (6, carry1)\n\n0+4=4 +1=5\n\n4+8=12 (2, carry1)\n\n8 (ten millions place) +3 (ten millions in second number) = 11 +1 (carry) =12 (2, carry1)\n\n8 (hundred millions place) +5 (hundred millions in second number) =13 +1 (carry) =14 (4, carry1)\n\nSo total here would be 142,256,076.\n\nThen adding to the 1,300M:\n\n1,300,000,000 +142,256,076 = 1,442,256,076. Okay that matches. So the answer is correct.\n\nSo the final sum is 1,442,256,076.\n</think>", '']
