 million plus 99,234.\n\n125,931,556 is 125 million plus 931,556.\n\nAdding the millions parts: 967 + 125 = 1,092 million.\n\nNow the remaining parts: 99,234 + 931,556.\n\nAdding those: 99,234 + 931,556.\n\n99,234 + 931,556 = let's see:\n\n99,234 + 900,000 = 999,234.\n\nThen add 31,556: 999,234 + 31,556 = 1,030,790.\n\nSo total sum is 1,092,000,000 + 1,030,790 = 1,093,030,790. That matches the previous result.\n\nSo the answer should be 1,093,030,790.\n\nWait, but in the digit-by-digit breakdown earlier, the digits are 1 0 9 3 0 3 0 7 9 0, which is 1,093,030,790. Yes. So that's correct.\n\nSo the final answer is 1,093,030,790.\n\nBut let me check once more with another approach, perhaps using column addition:\n\nLet me write both numbers:\n\n  967,099,234\n\n+ 125,931,556\n\n------------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:4+6=10 \u21920, carryover1.\n\nTens:3+5=8 +1=9.\n\nHundreds:2+5=7.\n\nThousands:9+1=10 \u21920, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:9+3=12 +1=13 \u21923, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:0+9=9 +1=10 \u21920, carryover1.\n\nMillions:7+5=12 +1=13 \u21923, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:6+2=8 +1=9.\n\nHundred millions:9+1=10 \u21920, carryover1.\n\nBillions:1 (from carryover).\n\nSo writing all digits with the carries, the total is 1,093,030,790. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 1,093,030,790.\n\n</think>\n\n",
