umber has4, second has4. 4+4=8 +1=9, carryover0.\n\nHundred millions:6+1=7.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:8,\n\nTens:1,\n\nHundreds:9,\n\nThousands:3,\n\nTen thousands:9,\n\nHundred thousands:6,\n\nMillions:6,\n\nTen millions:9,\n\nHundred millions:7.\n\nSo the total is 796,969, 318? Wait the commas would be:\n\n7 (hundred millions),\n\n9 (ten millions),\n\n6 (millions),\n\n6 (hundred thousands),\n\n9 (ten thousands),\n\n3 (thousands),\n\n9 (hundreds),\n\n1 (tens),\n\n8 (ones).\n\nSo written as 796,969,318? But when I did the alternative addition, I had 796,693,918. There's a discrepancy here. Hmm. Let me check with another method.\n\nWait, maybe my alternative addition was wrong. Let me recalculate the alternative method step by step.\n\nFirst number:647,958,859.\n\nSecond number:148,735,059.\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me add 647,958,859 + 148,735,059.\n\nLet me break into parts:\n\n647,958,859 + 100,000,000 = 747,958,859.\n\nThen add 48,735,059 to 747,958,859.\n\n747,958,859 +48,735,059.\n\nLet's break this down further:\n\n747,958,859 +40,000,000 = 787,958,859.\n\nNow add 8,735,059:\n\n787,958,859 +8,000,000 = 795,958,859.\n\nNow add 735,059:\n\n795,958,859 +700,000 = 796,658,859.\n\nThen add 35,059:\n\n796,658,859 +35,000 = 796,693,859.\n\nThen add 59: 796,693,859 +59 =796,693,918.\n\nWait, so according to this method, it's 796,693,918.\n\nBut according to the digit-by-digit, it's 796,969,318.\n\nThere's a discrepancy in the millions and hundred thousands places. Let me check where I went wrong.\n\nLooking back at the digit-by-digit:\n\nPosition7 (millions place):\n\nFirst number's millions digit is7, second is8. So 7+8=15 plus carryover1 (from position6 which had 16, so carryover1) →15+1=16. So digit6, carryover1. So that's correct.\n\nPosition7 (millions) digit is6. So in the total, the millions place is6. But in the alternative method, the millions place comes from the 7 (original 647 million) plus 148 million, so 647+148=795, so