\nDigit 1: 9 (hundred millions place?)\n\nWait, in a 9-digit number, the places are:\n\nDigit 1: hundred millions\n\nDigit 2: ten millions\n\nDigit3: millions\n\nDigit4: hundred thousands\n\nDigit5: ten thousands\n\nDigit6: thousands\n\nDigit7: hundreds\n\nDigit8: tens\n\nDigit9: ones.\n\nWait, no, perhaps the first digit is the highest place. Let\'s confirm:\n\nTake 925,779,816.\n\nBreaking down:\n\n- 925,779,816: The first part "925" is in millions. So:\n\n925,779,816 = 925,000,000 + 779,816.\n\nSo the digits:\n\nDigit 1 (hundred millions):9\n\nDigit2 (ten millions):2\n\nDigit3 (millions):5\n\nDigit4 (hundred thousands):7\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):7\n\nDigit6 (thousands):9\n\nDigit7 (hundreds):8\n\nDigit8 (tens):1\n\nDigit9 (ones):6\n\nSecond number: 324,353,227.\n\nBreaking down similarly:\n\n324,353,227 = 324,000,000 + 353,227.\n\nDigits:\n\nDigit1 (hundred millions):3\n\nDigit2 (ten millions):2\n\nDigit3 (millions):4\n\nDigit4 (hundred thousands):3\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):5\n\nDigit6 (thousands):3\n\nDigit7 (hundreds):2\n\nDigit8 (tens):2\n\nDigit9 (ones):7\n\nNow, let\'s add digit by digit from right (ones place) to left:\n\nStarting with Digit9 (ones place):\n\nFirst number:6, second:7 → 6+7=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\n\nDigit8 (tens):\n\nFirst:1, second:2 →1+2=3, plus carryover 1 →4. Write 4, carryover 0.\n\nDigit7 (hundreds):\n\nFirst:8, second:2 →8+2=10. Write 0? Wait 8+2=10? Wait first number\'s hundreds digit is 8, second is 2. 8+2=10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nWait, but I thought earlier the hundreds digit of first number is 8, second is 2. So 8+2=10. So yes, 0 and carryover1.\n\nWait, but in my previous step-by-step, I had thought the hundreds digit was 1 for first number, which was wrong. That was my mistake earlier. So need to correct that.\n\nContinuing:\n\nDigit7 (hundreds):\n\n8 +2 =10 + carryover 0 (since previous step had no carryover after tens place). Wait wait, after the tens place, we had a carryover of 0, right? The tens place was 1+2+1 