ition9:5,\n\nPosition8:2,\n\nPosition7:2,\n\nPosition6:9,\n\nPosition5:1,\n\nPosition4:5,\n\nPosition3:5,\n\nPosition2:1,\n\nPosition1:9.\n\nThus, the number is 5 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),5 (hundreds),1 (tens),9 (ones). So written out: 522,915,519.\n\nWait, so my initial calculation had a mistake when I first thought 522,915,159. The thousands place is 5, and the hundreds place is also 5. So the correct sum should be 522,915,519.\n\nHmm, so I need to make sure I didn't mix up the digits. Let me verify with another method, perhaps adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, let's add 110,648,257 and 412,267,262.\n\nFirst, adding the millions:\n\n110,648,257 is 110 million plus 648,257.\n\n412,267,262 is 412 million plus 267,262.\n\nAdding the millions: 110 + 412 = 522 million.\n\nNow adding the remaining parts: 648,257 + 267,262.\n\nLet's compute that:\n\n648,257 + 267,262.\n\nAdding the thousands:\n\n600,000 + 200,000 = 800,000.\n\n48,000 + 67,000 = 115,000 \u2192 total so far: 915,000.\n\nThen 257 + 262 = 519.\n\nSo total of the smaller parts: 915,000 + 519 = 915,519.\n\nTherefore, total sum is 522,000,000 + 915,519 = 522,915,519.\n\nOkay, so that matches the digit-by-digit result. So the correct answer should be 522,915,519.\n\nI must have made a mistake in my initial thought when I thought 522,915,159. Probably mixed up the thousands and hundreds places. So the final answer is indeed 522,915,519.\n\nSo to structure the reasoning properly as per the template:\n\n1. Ones place: 7 + 2 = 9.\n\n2. Tens place: 5 + 6 = 11, write down 1, carry over 1.\n\n3. Hundreds place: 2 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 5.\n\n4. Thousands place: 8 + 7 = 15, write 5, carry over 1.\n\n5. Ten thousands place: 4 + 6 + 1 (carry) = 11, write 1, carry over 1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place: 6 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 9.\n\n7. Millions place: 0 + 2 = 2.\n\n8. Ten millions place: 1 + 1 = 2.\n\n9. Hundred millions place: 1 + 4 = 5.\n\nSo the digits are 5 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),5 (hundreds),1 (tens),9 (ones). So the final answer is 522,915,519.\n\nI should make sure that in the reasoning steps, each digit is clearly noted. The problem might expect the steps written out in the order of places (ones, tens, etc.), so following that structure.\n</think>\n\n",
