e digits from right to left are:\n\nOnes:1,\n\nTens:0,\n\nHundreds:1,\n\nThousands:7,\n\nTen thousands:5,\n\nHundred thousands:9,\n\nMillions:7,\n\nTen millions:0,\n\nHundred millions:4,\n\nBillions:1.\n\nSo arranging from left to right (billions first): 1,4,0,7,9,5,7,1,0,1.\n\nWait, that would be 1,407,957,101. But when I added the millions and the remaining parts, I got 1,407,777,101. So which is correct?\n\nWait let me recalculate the second method:\n\nWait 570,639,241 + 837,137,860.\n\nBreaking into parts:\n\n570,639,241 = 500,000,000 + 70,000,000 + 600,000 + 30,000 + 9,000 + 200 + 40 +1.\n\n837,137,860 = 800,000,000 + 30,000,000 + 7,000,000 + 100,000 + 30,000 + 7,000 + 800 +60 +0.\n\nAdding the hundreds of millions:\n\n500M +800M =1,300M.\n\nThen 70M +30M=100M \u2192 total so far 1,400M.\n\nThen 600k +7,000,000 \u2192 wait, perhaps this way is getting too confusing.\n\nAlternatively, let's add the two numbers digit by digit again.\n\nWait let's do it step by step:\n\nNumber1:570,639,241.\n\nNumber2:837,137,860.\n\nAligning:\n\nPosition 1 (ones):1+0=1.\n\nPosition2 (tens):4+6=10 \u2192 0 carry1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):2+8=10 +1=11 \u21921 carry1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9+7=16 +1=17 \u21927 carry1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):3+1=4 +1=5 \u21925 no carry.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):6+3=9 \u21929 no carry.\n\nPosition7 (millions):0+7=7 \u21927 no carry.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):7+3=10 \u21920 carry1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5+8=13 +1=14 \u21924 carry1.\n\nThen the final carryover1, so total is 1,407,957,101.\n\nWait in my second method earlier, I must have made an error. Let me recalculate that approach:\n\nFirst, breaking into millions and the rest:\n\n570,639,241 = 570,000,000 + 639,241.\n\n837,137,860 =837,000,000 + 137,860.\n\nAdding the millions:570M +837M =1,407M.\n\nAdding the smaller parts:639,241 +137,860.\n\n639,241 +137,860:\n\nLet's add 639,241 + 100,000 =739,241.\n\nThen add 37,860: 739,241 +37,860 = 777,101.\n\nSo total sum is1,40