ition7:7,\n\nPosition6:1,\n\nPosition5:3,\n\nPosition4:7,\n\nPosition3:8,\n\nPosition2:6,\n\nPosition1:0.\n\nSo when adding digit by digit from the right (position1 to position9):\n\nPosition1:1+0=1.\n\nPosition2:4+6=10 →0, carry1.\n\nPosition3:2+8=10 +1=11 →1, carry1.\n\nPosition4:9+7=16 +1=17 →7, carry1.\n\nPosition5:3 (from first number) +3 (from second) =6 +1 (carry)=7 →7, no carry.\n\nPosition6:6 (first) +1 (second) =7 →7, no carry.\n\nPosition7:0 (first) +7 (second)=7 →7, no carry.\n\nPosition8:7 (first) +3 (second)=10 →0, carry1.\n\nPosition9:5 (first) +8 (second)=13 +1 (carry)=14 →4, carry1.\n\nThen the final carryover1.\n\nSo the digits from position1 to position9 plus the carryover give:\n\nCarryover1, then the digits from position9 to 1:\n\nPosition9:4,\n\nPosition8:0,\n\nPosition7:7,\n\nPosition6:7,\n\nPosition5:7,\n\nPosition4:7,\n\nPosition3:1,\n\nPosition2:0,\n\nPosition1:1.\n\nWait let me list them properly:\n\nThe final digits are:\n\nCarryover1 (position10),\n\nPosition9:4,\n\nPosition8:0,\n\nPosition7:7,\n\nPosition6:7,\n\nPosition5:7,\n\nPosition4:7,\n\nPosition3:1,\n\nPosition2:0,\n\nPosition1:1.\n\nSo the number is 1,407,777,101.\n\nWait aha! So earlier in my first calculation, I had a mistake in the position5 and position6 digits. Let me see.\n\nWait in the first calculation, I thought position5 (ten thousands place):\n\nFirst number's digit5:3,\n\nSecond number's digit5:1? Wait no, wait in the second number, the fifth digit from the right is 3.\n\nWait let me re-express:\n\nFirst number's digits (from position1 to 9):\n\n1,4,2,9,3,6,0,7,5.\n\nSecond number's digits (position1 to9):\n\n0,6,8,7,3,1,7,3,8.\n\nWait maybe my previous breakdown was incorrect.\n\nWait let's do it again carefully:\n\nFirst number:570,639,241.\n\nBreaking down digit by digit from right (ones) to left (billions):\n\nPosition1 (ones):1,\n\nPosition2 (tens):4,\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):2,\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9,\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):3,\n\nPosition6 (hundred tho