      "text": "1,067,646,744? Wait, let me verify with another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\n436,064,957\n\n+631,579,777\n\nLet me add them:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7+7 =14. 4, carryover1.\n\n5+7=12 +1=13. 3, carryover1.\n\n9+9=18 +1=19. 9, carryover1.\n\n4+7=11 +1=12. 2, carryover1.\n\n6+9=15 +1=16. 6, carryover1.\n\n0+5=5 +1=6. No carryover.\n\n6+1=7.\n\n3+3=6.\n\n4+6=10. So 0 with carryover1.\n\nAdding the final carryover gives 1 at the beginning.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\n1 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands?), wait wait wait, there might be a discrepancy here.\n\nWait in the thousands place, earlier steps had 4 (first number) +9 (second number's thousands digit) =13 plus carryover 1 makes 14. So that would be 4 in thousands place, carryover1. But in this quick addition, I thought 4+7=11? Wait, no, confusion again.\n\nWait let's do it step by step again with this method.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:\n\n          436,064,957\n\n        + 631,579,777\n\n        -----------------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digits:\n\nOnes place: 7+7=14. Write 4, carryover1.\n\nTens place:5+7=12 +1=13. Write3, carryover1.\n\nHundreds place:9+7=16 +1=17. Write7, carryover1.\n\nThousands place:4 (from first number) +9 (from second number's thousands digit)=13 +1=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands place:6 (first number's ten thousands) +7 (second number's ten thousands)=13 +1=14. Write4, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands place:0 +5=5 +1=6. Write6, no carryover.\n\nMillions place:6 (first number's millions digit) +1 (second number's millions digit)=7. Write7.\n\nTen millions place:3 +3=6. Write6.\n\nHundred millions place:4 +6=10. Write0, carryover1.\n\nThe final carryover adds a 1 in the billions place.\n\nSo the result is 1,067,646,744.\n\nYes, that matches the previous result. So the final sum should be 1,067,646,744.\n\nWait but let me che