nWait, but earlier I thought ten thousands place was 4 for first number. So 4+8=12, so yes.\n\nHundred thousands place:8 (from first number) +1 (from second number's hundred thousands place) + carryover 1. Wait, let me check:.\n\nWait the first number's hundred thousands digit is 8 (from 505,840,948: the part after 505 is 840, so 8 in hundred thousands, 4 in ten thousands, 0 in thousands). The second number's hundred thousands place is 1 (from 315,185,871: the part after 315 is 185, so 1 in hundred thousands, 8 in ten thousands, 5 in thousands). So 8+1=9 plus the carryover 1 makes 10. So write 0 and carryover1.\n\nMillions place:5 (from first number's millions place) +5 (second's millions place) + carryover1. Wait first number's millions digit is 5 (the third digit from the left in 505,840,948), and second's is 5 (third digit in 315,185,871). So 5+5=10 plus 1 is 11. So write 1, carryover1.\n\nTen millions place:0 (first number's ten millions) +1 (second's ten millions) +1 (carryover) = 2. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nHundred millions place:5 +3 =8. Write 8.\n\nPutting all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:9.\n\nTens:1 (with carryover).\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:2 (with carryover).\n\nHundred thousands:0 (with carryover).\n\nMillions:1 (with carryover).\n\nTen millions:2.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nSo combining all digits from left to right: 8 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 9 (ones). Wait, let me check again step by step.\n\nWait the digits in each place:.\n\nHundred millions:5+3=8.\n\nTen millions:0+1=1 + carryover? Wait no. Let me go step by step again, maybe I messed up in the order.\n\nWait let's do each digit step by step properly:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n1. Ones: 8 +1 =9 → 9. No carryover.\n\n2. Tens:4 +7=11 → 1, carryover 1.\n\n3. Hundreds:9 +8=17 +1=18 →8, carryover1.\n\n4. Thousands:0 +5=5 +1=6 →6, no carryover.\n\n5. Ten thousands:4 (first number) +8 (second number) =12 →2, carryover1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:8 (first) +1 (second) =9 +1 (carryover) =10 →0, carryover1.\n\n7. Millions:5 (first) +5 (second) =10 +1 (carryover)=11 →1, carryover1.\n\n8. Ten millions:0 (first) +1 (second) =1 +1 (carryover)=2 →2, no carryover.\n\n9. Hundred millions:5 (first) +3 (second) =8 →8.\n\nSo putting all digits from highest to lowest (hundred millions to ones):.\n\n8 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 9 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
