thousands):\n\n8 +6 =14 +1=15. Sum digit:5, carryover=1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):\n\n3 +4 =7 +1=8. Sum digit:8, carryover=0.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):\n\n2 +8 =10 +0=10. Sum digit:0, carryover=1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):\n\n8 +5 =13 +1=14. Sum digit:4, carryover=1.\n\nNow, after the last digit (position9), there's a carryover of1, so we add a new digit at the billions place: 1.\n\nThus, the total sum is:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:4\n\nTen millions:0\n\nMillions:8\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:2\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:4\n\nOnes:0\n\nSo arranging the digits from highest to lowest place:\n\n1 (billion), 4 (hundred million), 0 (ten million), 8 (million), 5 (hundred thousand),4 (ten thousand),2 (thousand),9 (hundred),4 (ten),0 (one).\n\nThus the number is 1,408,542,940.\n\nBut this contradicts the other method which gave 1,388,742,940. Which one is correct?\n\nLet me check with another approach: using calculator-like addition.\n\nLet me compute 823,866,285 + 564,876,655.\n\nBreak it into smaller parts:\n\nLet me add 823,866,285 + 500,000,000 =1,323,866,285.\n\nThen add 64,876,655:\n\n1,323,866,285 +60,000,000 =1,383,866,285.\n\nThen +4,876,655:\n\n1,383,866,285 +4,000,000 =1,387,866,285.\n\nThen +876,655:\n\n1,387,866,285 +800,000 =1,388,666,285.\n\nThen +76,655:\n\n1,388,666,285 +70,000 =1,388,736,285.\n\nThen +6,655:\n\n1,388,736,285 +6,000 =1,388,742,285.\n\nThen +655: 1,388,742,285 +655 =1,388,742,940.\n\nAh! So this method gives 1,388,742,940, which matches the first method's result. Therefore, the digit-by-digit approach must have an error.\n\nLooking back at the digit-by-digit steps, where did I go wrong?\n\nLet me re-examine the digit positions and their corresponding numbers.\n\nFirst number: 823,866,285.\n\nBreaking down each digit from right (position1):\n\nPosition1:5 (ones)\n\nPosition2:8 (tens)\n\nPosition3:2 (hundreds)\n\nPosition4:6 (thousands)\n\nPosition5:6 (ten thousands)\n\nPosition6:8 (hundred thousands)\n\n