usands):.\n\n1 +8 =9 →9, carry0.\n\nPosition3 (millions):.\n\n4 (first) +9 (second) =13 →3, carry1.\n\nPosition2 (ten millions):.\n\n3 (first) +7 (second) +1 (carry) =11 →1, carry1.\n\nPosition1 (hundred millions):.\n\n7 (first) +9 (second) +1 (carry) =17 →7, carry1.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 1 after the hundred millions place, we need to add a new digit to the left (billions place): 1.\n\nSo the total sum digits from right to left are:.\n\nPositions:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:7.\n\nTen millions:1.\n\nMillions:3.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:7.\n\nThousands:3.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nTens:1.\n\nOnes:0.\n\nSo writing that out from left to right (billions first):.\n\n1 (billion), 7 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 0 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
