s 3\n\nPosition5: ten thousands 0\n\nPosition6: hundred thousands 6\n\nPosition7: millions 0\n\nPosition8: ten millions 5\n\nPosition9: hundred millions 6\n\nSo combining from highest to lowest place:\n\nHundred millions (position9):6,\n\nten millions (position8):5,\n\nmillions (position7):0,\n\nhundred thousands (position6):6,\n\nten thousands (position5):0,\n\nthousands (position4):3,\n\nhundreds (position3):0,\n\ntens (position2):5,\n\nones (position1):1.\n\nWait, that would be 650,603,051. Yes, that's the same as before. So I think that's correct. I was worried I might have messed up a digit somewhere, but both methods give the same result. So I feel confident the answer is 650,603,051.",
