,138,124 \u2192 1,650,138,124.\n\nAh! The difference is in the hundred thousands and ten thousands places: in the first method, it's 318 thousand, but in the other it's 138 thousand. So that's a difference of 180 thousand.\n\nWait where is this coming from?\n\nWait let me re-express the two totals:\n\nDigit-wise full addition:1,650,318,124.\n\nOther method:1,650,138,124.\n\nThe difference between these two is 1,650,318,124 -1,650,138,124 =180,000. So the digit-wise addition has an extra 180,000.\n\nThis must be due to an error in the digit-wise addition process.\n\nLet me re-express the digit-wise steps again carefully:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position1):\n\nPosition1 (ones):7+7=14 \u21924, carry1.\n\nPosition2 (tens):5+6=11+1=12 \u21922, carry1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1+9=10+1=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):3+4=7+1=8 \u21928, carry0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):7+6=13 \u21923, carry1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):4+6=10+1=11 \u21921, carry1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):4+5=9+1=10 \u21920, carry1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):7+7=14+1=15 \u21925, carry1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):8+7=15+1=16 \u21926, carry1.\n\nPosition10 (billions): carry1 \u21921.\n\nSo the digits from position1 to position10 are:\n\n4,2,1,8,3,1,0,5,6,1.\n\nArranged as:\n\nPosition10 (billions):1,\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):6,\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):5,\n\nPosition7 (millions):0,\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):1,\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):3,\n\nPosition4 (thousands):8,\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1,\n\nPosition2 (tens):2,\n\nPosition1 (ones):4.\n\nSo the number is indeed 1,650,318,124.\n\nBut the other method says 1,650,138,124.\n\nWait why the discrepancy? Let me recheck the other method.\n\nOriginal numbers:874,473,157 +775,664,967.\n\nBreaking into 800,000,000 +700,000,000 =1,500,000,000.\n\nRemaining parts:74,473,157 +75,664,967.\n\nWait 74,473,157 +75,664,967 =150,138,124.\n\nAdding to 1,500,000,000 gives 1,650,138,124.\n\nWait, but 74,473,157 +75,