s), 5 (hundred-thousands), 9 (ten-thousands), 4 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 5 (ones). Wait, let me check that again because when I added the ten-millions place, I had 4+8+1=13, so the ten-millions digit is 3 and carry 1 to the hundred-millions. The hundred-millions digits were 3 and 4, so 3+4=7 plus the 1 makes 8. So the digits from left to right would be 8,3,3,5,9,4,6,2,5. So the total is 833,594,625? Wait, let me verify with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should add them step by step more carefully. Let me write it out vertically again, column by column with the carries:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place:.\n5 + 0 =5.\n\nTens place:.\n9 + 3 =12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nHundreds place:.\n7 + 8 =15 +1=16 →6, carry1.\n\nThousands place:.\n9 +4 =13 +1=14 →4, carry1.\n\nTen-thousands:.\n4 +4 =8 +1=9 →9, no carry.\n\nHundred-thousands:.\n5 +0 =5 →5.\n\nMillions:.\n6 +7 =13 →3, carry1.\n\nTen-millions:.\n4 +8 =12 +1=13 →3, carry1.\n\nHundred-millions:.\n3 +4 =7 +1=8 →8.\n\nSo the total is 833,594,625. Wait, but let me check if I have the positions right. Let me count the digits. Each number is 9 digits. 364,549,795 is 3 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 5 (ones). The second number is 487,044,830: 4 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),7 (millions),0 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),8 (hundreds),3 (tens),0 (ones). So when adding, the hundred millions digits are 3 +4 =7 plus the carry from the ten millions. Wait, in the previous step, when adding ten millions place (the 8th digit from the right?), let's see:.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the place values. Let me write each number with commas to see:.\n\nFirst number: 364,549,795 → 3,6,4,5,4,9,7,9,5.\n\nSecond number: 487,044,830 →4,8,7,0,4,4,8,3,0.\n\nWait, actually, the commas are placed every three digits. So 364,549,795 is split as 3 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 9 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 5 (ones). The second number 487,044,830 is 4 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),7 (millions),0 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),8 (hundreds),3 (tens),0 (ones).\n\nAdding them:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:5+0=5.\n\nTens:9+3=12 →2, carry1.\n\nHundreds:7+8=15 +1=16 →6, carry1.\n\nThousands:9+4=13 +1=14 →4, carry1.\n\nTen thousands:4 +4=8 +1=9 →9.\n\nHundred thousands:5 +0=5 →5.\n\nMillions:4 +7=11 →1? Wait, hold on. Wait, the millions place in the first number is 4 (since it's 3,6,4 in the first three digits). Wait no, wait, let me list all digits properly:.\n\nFirst number digits (from right to left, but let's list left to right):.\n\nFirst number: 3 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions),4 (millions),5 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),9 (thousands),7 (hundreds),9 (tens),5 (ones).\n\nSecond number:4 (hundred millions),8 (ten millions),7 (millions),0 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),8 (hundreds),3 (tens),0 (ones).\n\nWait, when adding the millions place (the 4th digit from the left?), actually, let's go step by step:.\n\nLet me list each digit position from right (ones) to left (hundred millions):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):5 +0 =5.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):9 +3=12 →2 carry1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):7 +8=15 +1=16 →6 carry1.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9 (from first number's thousands place) +4 (from second number's thousands place)=13 +1=14 →4 carry1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):4 (first) +4 (second)=8 +1=9 →9.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5 (first) +0 (second)=5 →5.\n\nPosition7 (millions):4 (first number's millions digit is the 4th digit from left? Wait, let me see:.\n\nWait, the first number's digits in order are:.\n\nDigit 1 (leftmost):3 (hundred millions).\n\nDigit 2:6 (ten millions).\n\nDigit3:4 (millions).\n\nDigit4:5 (hundred thousands).\n\nDigit5:4 (ten thousands).\n\nDigit6:9 (thousands).\n\nDigit7:7 (hundreds).\n\nDigit8:9