87.\nBreaking down:.\n- 9 (hundred millions).\n- 0 (ten millions).\n- 3 (millions).\n- 9 (hundred thousands).\n- 8 (ten thousands).\n- 9 (thousands).\n- 3 (hundreds).\n- 8 (tens).\n- 7 (ones).\n\nWait, so when adding, let's line them up properly:.\n\n          8 5 1 0 8 6 4 2 7.\n        + 9 0 3 9 8 9 3 8 7.\n        ---------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n7 + 7 = 14 → 4, carry 1.\n\nTens: 2 + 8 = 10, plus 1 = 11 → 1, carry 1.\n\nHundreds: 4 + 3 = 7 + 1 (carry) = 8 → 8, no carry.\n\nThousands place: 6 + 9 = 15 → 5, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands: 8 + 8 = 16 + 1 = 17 → 7, carry 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 0 + 9 = 9 +1 =10 → 0, carry 1.\n\nMillions place: 1 (from first number) + 3 (from second) =4 +1 (carry) =5 → 5, no carry.\n\nTen millions place: 5 (first) + 0 (second) =5 → 5.\n\nHundred millions place: 8 +9=17 → 7, carry 1.\n\nWait, but the hundred millions digits are 8 and 9. 8+9=17, so we write 7 and carry over 1. But there's no higher place, so that 1 becomes a new digit at the billions place.\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum would be:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:4.\n\nTens:1.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nTen thousands:7.\n\nHundred thousands:0.\n\nMillions:5.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nHundred millions:7, plus the carried 1 in the billions place: 1.\n\nSo the total is 1,755,078,514?.\n\nWait let me check again step by step.\n\nWait, let's do this step by step again carefully.\n\nFirst number: 851,086,427.\n\nSecond number:903,989,387.\n\nAdding digit by digit from right:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):7+7=14 → 4, carry 1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):2+8=10 +1=11 →1, carry1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):4+3=7 +1=8 →8, no carry.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):6+9=15 →5, carry1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):8+8=16 +1=17 →7, carry1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):0+9=9 +1=10 →0, carry1.\n\nPosition7 (millions):1+3=4 +1=5 →5, no carry.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):5+0=5 →5, no carry.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):8+9=17 →7, carry1.\n\nNow, the carried 1 goes to the next position (billions place), which is a new digit. So the total becomes 1,755,078,514?.\n\nWait, let me reconstruct the digits:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\nPositions (from right):.\n\n1:4.\n\n2:1.\n\n3:8.\n\n4:5.\n\n5:7.\n\n6:0.\n\n7:5.\n\n8:5.\n\n9:7.\n\nThen the carried 1 at the 10th position (billions).\n\nSo writing the number:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:7.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nMillions:5.\n\nHundred thousands:0.\n\nTen thousands:7.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nHundreds:5.\n\nTens:1.\n\nOnes:4.\n\nWait, that would be 1,755,078,514? Let me see:.\n\nBreaking down the digits:.\n\nBillions place:1.\n\nHundred millions:7 → 170,000,000?.\n\nWait, no. Wait, the digits:.\n\nAfter adding, the digits from right to left (positions 1 to 9 plus the carry):.\n\nThe digits are:.\n\nPosition1 (ones):4.\n\nPosition2 (tens):1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):8.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):5.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):7.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):0.\n\nPosition7 (millions):5.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):5.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):7.\n\nPlus the carried 1 in the billions place:1.\n\nSo the number is:.\n\n1 (billions), 7 (hundred millions),5 (ten millions),5 (millions),0 (hundred thousands),7 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),5 (hundreds),1 (tens),4 (ones).\n\nWait that would be 1,755,078,514?.\n\nYes. Let's confirm with another method. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nAlternatively, adding 851,086,427 + 903,989,387.\n\nLet me compute 851,086,427 + 900,000,000 = 1,751,086,427. Then add the remaining 3,989,387.\n\n1,751,086,427 + 3,989,387 = ?.\n\nAdding 1,751,086,427 + 3,000,000 = 1,754,086,427.\n\nThen add 989,387: 1,754,086,427 + 989,387.\n\nAdding 900,000 gives 1,754,986,427</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
