otal is 900,000,000 +117,310,483 =1,017,310,483.\n\nThis suggests that the digit-wise approach is wrong.\n\nWait, where is the mistake in the digit-wise approach?\n\nLooking at the digit-wise result: 1,008,310,483 versus 1,017,310,483.\n\nThe difference is in the millions place. The digit-wise approach has 8 in millions place, while the breakdown has 17, so millions place would be 7?\n\nWait, let's look at the digit-wise breakdown:\n\nPosition7 (millions place) for the first number is4, and second is4. 4+4=8 \u2192 that's correct.\n\nBut in the breakdown method, the sum of the millions parts is 4 million +4 million =8 million. But in the total breakdown, the millions are part of the 43 million and 74 million.\n\nWait, perhaps the confusion is arising because the millions in the breakdown are part of larger numbers.\n\nWait, perhaps the digit-wise calculation is correct and the breakdown method is wrong.\n\nWait, let's take the digit-wise result 1,008,310,483 and subtract the first number to see if we get the second number.\n\n1,008,310,483 -643,193,619 = ?\n\n1,008,310,483 -600,000,000 =408,310,483.\n\nThen subtract 43,193,619:\n\n408,310,483 -43,193,619.\n\n408,310,483 -40,000,000 =368,310,483.\n\n-3,193,619 \u2192 368,310,483 -3,193,619 =365,116,864.\n\nWhich is not equal to the second number (374,116,864). So there's an inconsistency.\n\nThus, the digit-wise method must be incorrect.\n\nAlternatively, let's do the subtraction of the breakdown result:\n\n1,017,310,483 -643,193,619 = ?\n\n1,017,310,483 -600,000,000 =417,310,483.\n\nSubtract 43,193,619:\n\n417,310,483 -40,000,000 =377,310,483.\n\n-3,193,619 \u2192377,310,483 -3,193,619 =374,116,864.\n\nWhich matches the second number. Thus, the correct answer is 1,017,310,483.\n\nThis means my digit-wise approach had an error.\n\nGoing back to the digit-wise addition:\n\nThe mistake must be in the digit positions.\n\nWait, let's re-express the digit positions carefully.\n\nFirst number:643,193,619.\n\nDigits from ri