wn:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 1.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 9.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 6.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 2.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 8.\n\nPosition 7 (millions): 0.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 8.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 5.\n\nNow, adding each position step by step, starting from position 1:.\n\nPosition 1: 4 +1 =5. Write down 5.\n\nPosition 2: 3 +1=4. Write 4.\n\nPosition 3: 8 +9=17. Oh, here we have a carryover. So write down 7, carryover 1.\n\nWait, but I need to remember the carryover for the next positions.\n\nWait, let me start over more carefully, keeping track of any carryover.\n\nStarting with Position 1 (ones):.\n\n4 +1 =5. No carryover. Result so far: 5.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):.\n\n3 +1 =4. No carryover. Now the number is 45.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):.\n\n8 +9 =17. So write 7, carryover 1. Now the result is 745.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):.\n\n0 +6 =6, plus the carryover 1 makes 7. So next digit 7. Result now 7745.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):.\n\n9 +2 =11, plus 0 carryover (since previous was 1, but that was handled in the thousands place). Wait, let me check again.\n\nWait, after Position 3 (hundreds place), the carryover is 1 to the thousands place.\n\nSo Position 4 (thousands):.\n\n0 (from first number) +6 (from second number) + 1 (carryover) =7. Correct.\n\nNow moving to Position 5 (ten thousands):.\n\nFirst number has 9, second has 2. 9+2=11. No carryover from the previous step. Wait, but the previous step (thousands) didn't have a carryover beyond the 1 already accounted for. So 9+2=11. That gives 1 in the current position and carryover 1 to the next.\n\nWait, so Position 5:.\n\n9 +2 =11. So write down 1 and carryover 1. So the result so far is 1 (ten thousands place), but we have to consider the carryover. So the digits now are:.\n\nAfter Position 5: the current digit is 1, and carryover 1. So the current total digits from right would be ..17745? Wait, maybe I need to track this step by s