housands),7 (thousands), 0 (hundreds),2 (tens),9 (ones). Wait, maybe I need to parse each digit correctly.\n\nWait, let me do this step by step:.\n\nFirst number: 935,098,308.\n\nBreaking down each digit from left to right:.\n\nBillions place (if any): since it's 9 digits, the first digit is hundred millions.\n\nDigits:.\n\n1. 9 (hundred millions).\n\n2. 3 (ten millions).\n\n3. 5 (millions).\n\n4. 0 (hundred thousands).\n\n5. 9 (ten thousands).\n\n6. 8 (thousands).\n\n7. 3 (hundreds).\n\n8. 0 (tens).\n\n9. 8 (ones).\n\nSecond number:953,607,029.\n\nDigits:.\n\n1. 9 (hundred millions).\n\n2.5 (ten millions).\n\n3.3 (millions).\n\n4.6 (hundred thousands).\n\n5.0 (ten thousands).\n\n6.7 (thousands).\n\n7.0 (hundreds).\n\n8.2 (tens).\n\n9.9 (ones).\n\nWait, so when adding, we need to add each corresponding place from right to left.\n\nLet me list each place step by step:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 8 (from first number) +9 (second) = 17 → 7, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):0 +2 =2 +1 =3 →3, carry 0.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):3 +0 =3 →3, carry 0.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):8 +7 =15 →5, carry 1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):9 +0 =9 +1 (carry) =10 →0, carry 1.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):0 +6 =6 +1 (carry) =7 →7, carry 0.\n\nPosition7 (millions):5 +3 =8 →8, carry 0.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):3 +5 =8 →8, carry 0.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):9 +9 =18 →8, carry 1.\n\nNow, since we have a carryover of 1 after the hundred millions place, we need to add a new digit at the billions place: 1.\n\nSo putting it all together from right to left:.\n\nThe digits would be:.\n\nBillions place:1.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nTen millions:8.\n\nMillions:8.\n\nHundred thousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:0.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nTens:3.\n\nOnes:7.\n\nWait, let me reconstruct the number step by step.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position1):.\n\nPosition1:7.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition3:3 (Wait no, let me recheck):.\n\nWait, let me list each position's result:.\n\nPosition 1:7.\n\nPosition2:3.\n\nPosition3:3 (from hundreds place: 3+0=3).\n\nPosition4:5 (thousands place 8+7=15, so 5 with carry).\n\nPosition5:0 (ten thousands place:9+0 +1 (carry)=10 →0).\n\nPosition6:7 (hundred thousands:0+6 +1 (carry from previous?) Wait, wait:.\n\nWait let's go step by step again:.\n\nAfter position5 (ten thousands):.\n\nPosition5:9+0 +1 (carry from position4)=10 → digit 0, carryover1.\n\nThen position6 (hundred thousands):.\n\n0 (from first number) +6 (second) + carryover1 (from position5) → 0+6=6 +1=7 → digit7, carryover0.\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\n\n5 (first) +3 (second)=8 → digit8, no carry.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\n\n3 (first) +5 (second)=8 → digit8, no carry.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\n\n9 (first) +9 (second)=18 → digit8, carryover1.\n\nThen the final carryover1 goes to the next (billions) place.\n\nSo the digits from billions down to ones are:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nTen millions:8.\n\nMillions:8.\n\nHundred thousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:0.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nTens:3.\n\nOnes:7.\n\nTherefore, combining these digits:.\n\n1 (billions), 8 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),8 (millions),7 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),3 (hundreds),3 (tens),7 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
