\n\nSo total of the smaller parts:1,000,000 +123,066 =1,123,066.\n\nAdding that to the millions total:934,000,000 +1,123,066 =935,123,066. Yep, same result.\n\nSo I think that's correct. So the final answer should be 935,123,066.\n\nWait, but in my initial digit-by-digit addition, the digits were 9 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (ones). So written as 935,123,066. Yes, that's correct. So I think that's the right answer.\n\nJust to be thorough, let me try adding column by column again step by step, writing each step down:\n\nNumbers:\n\n  275,769,705\n\n+659,353,361\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right (ones):\n\nOnes: 5 +1 =6. Write 6.\n\nTens: 0 +6 =6. Write 6.\n\nHundreds:7 +3 =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:9 +3 =12 +1 (carryover)=13. Write 3, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:6 +5 =11 +1=12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:7 +3=10 +1=11. Write1, carryover1.\n\nMillions:5 +9=14 +1=15. Write5, carryover1.\n\nTen millions:7 +5=12 +1=13. Write3, carryover1.\n\nHundred millions:2 +6=8 +1=9. Write9.\n\nSo the result is 935,123,066. Perfect, same as before. So I'm confident that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe sum of 275,769,705 and 659,353,361 is \\boxed{935123066}.\n</think>", '']
