 + 1 = 9\\)\n9. **Hundred millions place**: \\(8 + 6 = 14\\). Write down 4 and carry over 1.\n10. **Billions place**: The carried over 1.\n\nPutting all the digits together, we get the final sum as follows:\n\n- Billions place: 1\n- Hundred millions place: 4\n- Ten millions place: 9\n- Millions place: 2\n- Hundred thousands place: 6\n- Ten thousands place: 7\n- Thousands place: 9\n- Hundreds place: 3\n- Tens place: 4\n- Ones place: 8\n\nThus, the final computed sum is \\(\\boxed{1492679348}\\).", '']
