>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 425139044 and 363977421?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n\n1. The ones place: \\(4 + 1 = 5\\)\n2. The tens place: \\(4 + 2 = 6\\)\n3. The hundreds place: \\(0 + 7 = 7\\)\n4. The thousands place: \\(9 + 4 = 13\\) (Write down 3, carry over 1)\n5. The ten-thousands place: \\(3 + 7 + 1 = 11\\) (Write down 1, carry over 1)\n6. The hundred-thousands place: \\(1 + 9 + 1 = 11\\) (Write down 1, carry over 1)\n7. The millions place: \\(5 + 3 + 1 = 9\\)\n8. The ten-millions place: \\(2 + 6 = 8\\)\n9. The hundred-millions place: \\(4 + 3 = 7\\)\n\nPutting all the digits together, we get the final sum as 789,116,465.\n\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is \\boxed{789116465}.", '']
