s 904 million.., so the digits are 9 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 4 (millions), etc. The second number is 700,623,392, which is 700 million, so the digits are 7 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 0 (millions), then 6 (hundred thousands), etc. .\n\nSo when adding the hundred millions place: 9 (from first) +7 (from second) = 16. So we had that right. Then the billions place: since both are 9-digit numbers, the first has a 9 in the hundred millions (so the highest is 900 million), and the second is 700 million</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
