n\nTens: 8 + 2 = 10.\n\nOnes: 5 + 6 = 11.\n\nWait, but this is the total per column, but we have to add them step by step with carryover. Let me do this step by step properly, starting from the right (ones place):.\n\nStarting over:.\n\nOnes place:.\n\n5 + 6 = 11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens place:.\n\n8 + 2 = 10, plus carryover 1 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nHundreds place:.\n\n2 + 1 = 3, plus carryover 1 = 4. Write 4, no carryover.\n\nThousands place:.\n\n9 (from first number) + 2 (second number) = 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands place:.\n\n3 + 3 = 6, plus carryover 1 = 7. Write 7, no carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands place:.\n\n2 (first) + 3 (second) = 5. Write 5, no carryover.\n\nMillions place:.\n\n1 (first) + 2 (second) = 3. Write 3, no carryover.\n\nTen-millions place:.\n\n9 (first) + 3 (second) = 12. Write 2, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-millions place:.\n\n1 (first) + 2 (second) = 3, plus carryover 1 = 4. Write 4.\n\nPutting all the digits together from right to left:.\n\nStarting from the ones digit we had:.\n\nOnes:1.\n\nTens:1.\n\nHundreds:4.\n\nThousands:1.\n\nTen-thousands:7.\n\nHundred-thousands:5.\n\nMillions:3.\n\nTen-millions:2 (but wait, the ten millions place after adding had 9+3=12 plus carryover?).\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the order here. Let me write the result step by step.\n\nWait, let me try writing the addition step by step with the carryover:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nPosition 1 (Ones):.\n\n5 + 6 = 11 → 1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 2 (Tens):.\n\n8 + 2 = 10 + 1 = 11 → 1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 3 (Hundreds):.\n\n2 + 1 = 3 + 1 = 4 → 4, no carryover.\n\nPosition 4 (Thousands):.\n\n9 + 2 = 11 → 1, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 5 (Ten-thousands):.\n\n3 + 3 = 6 + 1 =7 →7, no carryover.\n\nPosition 6 (Hundred-thousands):.\n\n2 + 3 =5 →5, no carryover.\n\nPosition 7 (Millions):.\n\n1 +2 =3 →3, no carryover.\n\nPosition 8 (Ten-millions):.\n\n9 (from first number) +3 (second) =12 →2, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 9 (Hundred-millions):.\n\