y:.\n\nFirst number: 8 1 5 0 6 6 4 5 0.\n\nBut let's see:.\n\nWait actually, the first number is 815,066,450. Let's break down each digit position:.\n\nStarting from the right (units):.\n\nPosition 1 (units): 0.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):5.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):4.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):6.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):6.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):0.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):5.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):1.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):8.\n\nSecond number: 518,824,319.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nPosition 1:9.\n\nPosition 2:1.\n\nPosition3:3.\n\nPosition4:4.\n\nPosition5:2.\n\nPosition6:8.\n\nPosition7:8.\n\nPosition8:1.\n\nPosition9:5.\n\nWait, but the second number is 518,824,319. Let me count the digits:.\n\n5 (hundred millions place), 1 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),3 (hundreds),1 (tens),9 (ones). So:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):9.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):1.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):3.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):4.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):8.\n\nPosition7 (millions):8.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5.\n\nSo now adding each position:.\n\nStarting from position1 (ones):.\n\n0 +9 =9, no carryover.\n\nPosition2 (tens):5 +1=6, no carry.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):4+3=7, no carry.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):6+4=10. So write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):6 (from first) +2 (second) +1 (carry)= 9. So 9, no carry.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):0 +8=8, no carry.\n\nPosition7 (millions):5 (first) +8 (second) =13. So write 3, carryover 1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):1 (first) +1 (second) +1 (carry) =3. So 3, no carry.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):8 +5 =13. So write 3, carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, that carryover 1 becomes a new digit at the next higher place (billions place).\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right, the digits are:.\n\nPosition1:9.\n\nPosition2:6.\n\nPosition3:7.\n\nPosition4:0.\n\nPo