450 and 518,824,319, we add the numbers digit by digit from right to left, carrying over as needed:\n\n1. **Ones place**: \\(0 + 9 = 9\\)\n2. **Tens place**: \\(5 + 1 = 6\\)\n3. **Hundreds place**: \\(4 + 3 = 7\\)\n4. **Thousands place**: \\(6 + 4 = 10\\). Write down 0 and carry over 1.\n5. **Ten thousands place**: \\(6 + 2 + 1 = 9\\)\n6. **Hundred thousands place**: \\(0 + 8 = 8\\)\n7. **Millions place**: \\(5 + 8 = 13\\). Write down 3 and carry over 1.\n8. **Ten millions place**: \\(1 + 1 + 1 = 3\\)\n9. **Hundred millions place**: \\(8 + 5 = 13\\). Write down 3 and carry over 1.\n\nThe final carry-over of 1 is added to the billions place, resulting in the digits:\n\n- **Billions place**: 1\n- **Hundred millions place**: 3\n- **Ten millions place**: 3\n- **Millions place**: 3\n- **Hundred thousands place**: 8\n- **Ten thousands place**: 9\n- **Thousands place**: 0\n- **Hundreds place**: 7\n- **Tens place**: 6\n- **Ones place**: 9\n\nCombining all these digits, the final sum is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1333890769}\n\\]", '']
