ht (position 1 to 9):\n\nPositions:\n\n1 (units):3\n\n2 (tens):5\n\n3 (hundreds):4\n\n4 (thousands):9\n\n5 (ten thousands):5\n\n6 (hundred thousands):6\n\n7 (millions):8\n\n8 (ten millions):7\n\n9 (hundred millions):3\n\nSecond number:755,413,704 → digits:\n\n1 (units):4\n\n2 (tens):0\n\n3 (hundreds):7\n\n4 (thousands):3\n\n5 (ten thousands):1\n\n6 (hundred thousands):4\n\n7 (millions):5\n\n8 (ten millions):5\n\n9 (hundred millions):7\n\nNow adding each position:\n\nPosition 1: 3 +4=7.\n\nPosition2:5+0=5.\n\nPosition3:4+7=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nPosition4:9+3 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nPosition5:5+1 +1=7 →7, no carryover.\n\nPosition6:6+4=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nPosition7:8+5 +1=14 →4, carryover1.\n\nPosition8:7+5 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nPosition9:3+7 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nThen the carryover1 for the next digit (billions place):1.\n\nSo the digits from position1 to 10:\n\nPosition10 (billions):1.\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):1.\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):3.\n\nPosition7 (millions):4.\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):0.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):7.\n\nPosition4 (thousands):3.\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1.\n\nPosition2 (tens):5.\n\nPosition1 (units):7.\n\nSo the number is:\n\n1 (billions), 1 (hundred millions), 3 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 0 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 1 (hundreds),5 (tens),7 (units).\n\nWait, so that would be 1,134,073,157? Wait, let me write it as:\n\n1 (billion) → 1,000,000,000.\n\nThen 1 (hundred millions) → 100,000,000 → total so far 1,100,000,000.\n\n3 (ten millions) →30,000,000 → 1,130,000,000.\n\n4 (millions) →4,000,000 →1,134,000,000.\n\n0 (hundred thousands) →0 → stays.\n\n7 (ten thousands) →70,000 →1,134,070,000.\n\n3 (thousands) →3,000 →1,134,073,000.\n\n1 (hundreds) →100 →1,134,073,100.\n\n5 (tens) →50 →1,134,073,150.\n\n7 (units) →7 →1,134,073,157.\n\nAh! So the digit-by-digit was actually correct, but when I first did the digit breakdown, I must have miscounted the places. So the correct total is 1,134,07