nTo find the sum of 187,369,043 and 980,443,654, we add the numbers digit by digit from right to left, carrying over any excess as needed:\n\n1. **Ones place**: \\(3 + 4 = 7\\)\n2. **Tens place**: \\(4 + 5 = 9\\)\n3. **Hundreds place**: \\(0 + 6 = 6\\)\n4. **Thousands place**: \\(9 + 3 = 12\\) (write 2, carry over 1)\n5. **Ten thousands place**: \\(6 + 4 + 1 = 11\\) (write 1, carry over 1)\n6. **Hundred thousands place**: \\(3 + 4 + 1 = 8\\)\n7. **Millions place**: \\(7 + 0 = 7\\)\n8. **Ten millions place**: \\(8 + 8 = 16\\) (write 6, carry over 1)\n9. **Hundred millions place**: \\(1 + 9 + 1 = 11\\) (write 1, carry over 1)\n10. **Billions place**: The carried over 1.\n\nCombining all the digits from the highest place (billions) to the lowest (ones), we get the sum:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1167812697}\n\\]",
