over.\n\nHundred millions place (position9):2 +4 =6.\n\nSo the total is 6 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions),6 (millions), then 3 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands),3 (thousands),3 (hundreds),0 (tens),1 (ones). So 656,323,301.\n\nBut when I broke it into parts earlier, I got 656,341,301. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's add the two numbers numerically:\n\n211,964,427.\n\n+444,376,874.\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n211,964,427.\n\n+444,376,874.\n\n------------.\n\nAdding step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:7+4=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nTens:2+7=9 +1=10 →0, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:4+8=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nThousands:6+6=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:4+7=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands:9+3=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\nMillions:1+4=5 +1=6 →6, no carryover.\n\nTen millions:1+4=5 →5.\n\nHundred millions:2+4=6 →6.\n\nSo the total is 656,323,301.\n\nWait, but when I broke it into 211,964,427 +444,376,874 = (200,000,000 + 11,964,427) + (400,000,000 +44,376,874) = 600,000,000 + (11,964,427+44,376,874).\n\nWait, adding 11,964,427 and 44,376,874:\n\nLet me compute that again:\n\n11,964,427.\n\n+44,376,874.\n\nAdding units:\n\n7+4=11 →1, carryover1.\n\n2+7=9+1=10 →0, carryover1.\n\n4+8=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\n6+6=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\n4+7=11 +1=12 →2, carryover1.\n\n9+3=12 +1=13 →3, carryover1.\n\n1+4=5 +1=6 →6, no carryover.\n\nThe rest: since 11,964,427 is 11 million and 44,376,874 is 44 million. Adding the millions part:\n\n11 million +44 million is 55 million. Then the rest of the digits give 633,301? Wait:\n\nWait the result of 11,964,427 +44,376,874 should be 56,341,301?\n\nWait let's do it digit by digit:\n\n11,964,427 has digits:\n\nMillions:1 (position7), hundred thousands:9 (position6), ten thousands:6 (position5?), wait let me clarify:\n\nWait 11,964,427 is 11,964,427. Let's break it down:\n\nDigits from right:\n\nPosition1:7.\n\n2:2.\n\n3:4.\n\n4:4.\n\n5:6.\n\n6:9.\n\n7:1.\n\n