9 (ones).\n\nSimilarly, 315,228,599:.\n\n3 (hundred millions).\n\n1 (ten millions).\n\n5 (millions).\n\n2 (hundred thousands).\n\n2 (ten thousands).\n\n8 (thousands).\n\n5 (hundreds).\n\n9 (tens).\n\n9 (ones).\n\nSo when adding, align each column:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\nOnes:9 +9 =18 → 8, carryover 1.\n\nTens:2 +9 =11 +1=12 →2, carryover1.\n\nHundreds:5 +5 =10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nThousands:2 +8=10 +1=11 →1, carryover1.\n\nTen thousands:3 +2=5 +1=6 →6, no carryover.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +2=5 →5.\n\nMillions:2 +5=7 →7.\n\nTen millions:8 +1=9 →9.\n\nHundred millions:6 +3=9 →9.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again carefully:.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position 1, ones):.\n\nDigit 1 (ones):.\n\nFirst number:9, second number:9 → 9+9=18. Write 8, carryover 1.\n\nDigit 2 (tens):.\n\nFirst number:2, second number:9 →2+9=11 +1 (carry)=12. Write 2, carryover1.\n\nDigit3 (hundreds):.\n\nFirst number:5, second number:5 →5+5=10 +1=11 → write 1, carryover1.\n\nDigit4 (thousands):.\n\nFirst number:2, second number:8 →2+8=10 +1=11 → write1, carryover1.\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):.\n\nFirst number:3, second number:2 →3+2=5 +1=6 → write6, no carryover.\n\nDigit6 (hundred thousands):.\n\nFirst number:3, second number:2 →3+2=5 → write5.\n\nDigit7 (millions):.\n\nFirst number:2, second number:5 →2+5=7 → write7.\n\nDigit8 (ten millions):.\n\nFirst number:8, second number:1 →8+1=9 → write9.\n\nDigit9 (hundred millions):.\n\nFirst number:6, second number:3 →6+3=9 → write9.\n\nPutting all together from right to left (since we started from ones):.\n\nDigits collected are:.\n\nPosition1:8.\n\nPosition2:2.\n\nPosition3:1.\n\nPosition4:1.\n\nPosition5:6.\n\nPosition6:5.\n\nPosition7:7.\n\nPosition8:9.\n\nPosition9:9.\n\nWait, but when written in order, the final number should be from the highest digit to the lowest. So the digits from the highest (hundred millions) down are 9 (hundred millions), then 9 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 6 (te